mands/speckit/complete.md\n.skilled/commands/speckit/handoff.md\n.skilled/commands/speckit/implement.md\n.skilled/commands/speckit/plan.md\n.skilled/commands/speckit/resume.md\n.skilled/commands/speckit/save.md\n.skilled/commands/speckit/search.md\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/commands/create/agent.md\n.skilled/commands/create/benchmark.md\n.skilled/commands/create/changelog.md\n.skilled/commands/create/command.md\n.skilled/commands/create/diff.md\n.skilled/commands/create/feature-catalog.md\n.skilled/commands/create/goal.md\n.skilled/commands/create/manual-testing-playbook.md\n.skilled/commands/create/readme.md\n.skilled/commands/create/repo-rule.md\n.skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md\n.skilled/commands/create/skill-parent.md\n.skilled/commands/create/with-human-voice.md\n.skilled/commands/deep/research.md\n.skilled/commands/deep/review.md\n.skilled/commands/design/chart.md\n.skilled/commands/design/diagram.md\n.skilled/commands/design/extract.md\n.skilled/commands/doctor/agents-md.md\n.skilled/commands/doctor/ci.md\n.skilled/commands/doctor/deep-loop.md\n.skilled/commands/doctor/env.md\n.skilled/commands/doctor/git.md\n.skilled/commands/doctor/helper.md\n.skilled/commands/doctor/install.md\n.skilled/commands/doctor/mcp.md\n.skilled/commands/doctor/overlay.md\n.skilled/commands/doctor/runtime-mirrors.md\n.skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md\n.skilled/commands/doctor/sk-code.md\n.skilled/commands/doctor/sk-skill.md\n.skilled/commands/doctor/skill-advisor.md\n.skilled/commands/doctor/speckit.md\n.skilled/commands/doctor/symlink.md\n.skilled/commands/doctor/update.md\n.skilled/commands/local-skilled-alignment.md\n.skilled/commands/prompt/improve.md\n.skilled/commands/speckit/ai-council.md\n.skilled/commands/speckit/complete.md\n.skilled/commands/speckit/handoff.md\n.skilled/commands/speckit/implement.md\n.skilled/commands/speckit/plan.md\n.skilled/commands/speckit/resume.md\n.skilled/commands/speckit/save.md\n.skilled/commands/speckit/search.md\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && find .skilled/commands -maxdepth 2 -name '*.md' -not -path '*/scripts/*' -not -path '*/assets/*' | sort\"}"},"time":{"start":1794830094815,"end":1794830096499}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794830096538,"sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeKe3TiuKUBtJoOy","part":{"partID":"prt_1e435d4df001RfKZyxtlYP9Ax8","sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeKe3TiuKUBtJoOy","messageID":"msg_1e435c6ba001rBNTOGy4Yec319","type":"tool","id":"call_c7495768b96c475ea2564ea3","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \"Forty-four commands\\|Create (13)\\|Spec Kit (8)\\|/create:\" README.md | head -40"},"output":"269:Each kind also has a `/create` command for when you want the workflow directly. `/create:sk-skill` creates or updates a skill, and `/create:skill-parent` scaffolds a parent hub with its modes. `/create:agent` and `/create:command` cover agents and slash commands. `/create:readme`, `/create:changelog`, `/create:goal` and `/create:repo-rule` cover the documents around them. Every one runs with `:auto` or with `:confirm` to pause at each step.\n341:A spec folder can hold a goal file with the directive and the criteria that decide when the work is done. This hook binds a session to that file and injects a short slice of it, so the goal survives context resets. `/create:goal` writes the file. Claude Code and Codex use their own `/goal` command instead, and the spec workflows hand you the slice to paste. OpenCode manages the goal with `/goal-opencode`, Pi with `/goal-pi` and DSH with `/goal-dsh`. Cursor's `/goal-cursor` can only read a packet's goal.\n588:- **`@markdown`** writes docs from templates and runs the `/create:*` commands\n599:Forty-four commands ship in six groups in the [commands folder](.skilled/commands/). Each one is a Markdown file, and most hand their steps to a YAML workflow beside it.\n601:**Spec Kit (8).** `/speckit:complete`, `/speckit:plan`, `/speckit:implement`, `/speckit:resume`, `/speckit:save`, `/speckit:search`, `/speckit:handoff` and `/speckit:ai-council`. These run the spec workflow and its continuity, as [Everyday Workflows](#5--everyday-workflows) describes.\n603:**Create (13).** `/create:sk-skill`, `/create:skill-parent`, `/create:agent`, `/create:command`, `/create:readme`, `/create:changelog`, `/create:feature-catalog`, `/create:manual-testing-playbook`, `/create:goal`, `/create:benchmark`, `/create:diff`, `/create:repo-rule` and `/create:with-human-voice`. These scaffold or revise one kind of artifact to the sk-doc standards.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"269:Each kind also has a `/create` command for when you want the workflow directly. `/create:sk-skill` creates or updates a skill, and `/create:skill-parent` scaffolds a parent hub with its modes. `/create:agent` and `/create:command` cover agents and slash commands. `/create:readme`, `/create:changelog`, `/create:goal` and `/create:repo-rule` cover the documents around them. Every one runs with `:auto` or with `:confirm` to pause at each step.\n341:A spec folder can hold a goal file with the directive and the criteria that decide when the work is done. This hook binds a session to that file and injects a short slice of it, so the goal survives context resets. `/create:goal` writes the file. Claude Code and Codex use their own `/goal` command instead, and the spec workflows hand you the slice to paste. OpenCode manages the goal with `/goal-opencode`, Pi with `/goal-pi` and DSH with `/goal-dsh`. Cursor's `/goal-cursor` can only read a packet's goal.\n588:- **`@markdown`** writes docs from templates and runs the `/create:*` commands\n599:Forty-four commands ship in six groups in the [commands folder](.skilled/commands/). Each one is a Markdown file, and most hand their steps to a YAML workflow beside it.\n601:**Spec Kit (8).** `/speckit:complete`, `/speckit:plan`, `/speckit:implement`, `/speckit:resume`, `/speckit:save`, `/speckit:search`, `/speckit:handoff` and `/speckit:ai-council`. These run the spec workflow and its continuity, as [Everyday Workflows](#5--everyday-workflows) describes.\n603:**Create (13).** `/create:sk-skill`, `/create:skill-parent`, `/create:agent`, `/create:command`, `/create:readme`, `/create:changelog`, `/create:feature-catalog`, `/create:manual-testing-playbook`, `/create:goal`, `/create:benchmark`, `/create:diff`, `/create:repo-rule` and `/create:with-human-voice`. These scaffold or revise one kind of artifact to the sk-doc standards.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \\\"Forty-four commands\\\\|Create (13)\\\\|Spec Kit (8)\\\\|/create:\\\" README.md | head -40\"}"},"time":{"start":1794830095583,"end":1794830096538}}}}
