{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794830101307,"sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeKe3TiuKUBtJoOy","part":{"id":"prt_1e435eb3b001qhmIY8Sh27BdxA","sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeKe3TiuKUBtJoOy","messageID":"msg_1e435e0ed001BCd7k4RWjJCBZO","type":"step-start","snapshot":"05528263d614a2c6dc32246ba283c6496cb5833a"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794830107370,"sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeKe3TiuKUBtJoOy","part":{"partID":"prt_1e435fe63001TqURg4ece1UCmv","sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeKe3TiuKUBtJoOy","messageID":"msg_1e435e0ed001BCd7k4RWjJCBZO","type":"tool","id":"call_ffd7d31bf88c48c39d22fbe3","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"README.md","offset":580,"limit":70},"output":"Read file README.md, lines 580-649\n580: \n581: Eleven agents own focused roles. Their source lives in the shared agents folder, which OpenCode links to. Codex, Pi, DSH and Mistral Vibe carry copies generated from it. Claude Code keeps its own hand-carried copy, and Cursor and Devin link to that copy.\n582: \n583: - **`@orchestrate`** splits multi-step work, hands each part to a specialist and merges the results\n584: - **`@code`** writes and fixes code for the detected stack and proves it works before it says done\n585: - **`@context`** finds what is already known, from packet continuity first and code search second\n586: - **`@review`** reviews code without editing it and ranks findings by severity\n587: - **`@debug`** takes a fresh look at a bug after three failed attempts, from a clean handoff\n588: - **`@markdown`** writes docs from templates and runs the `/create:*` commands\n589: - **`@prompt-improver`** turns a high-stakes prompt into a checked, structured package\n590: - **`@design`** decides visual values and builds style references, charts and diagrams\n591: - **`@ai-council`** runs several AI viewpoints toward one vetted plan and never writes code\n592: - **`@deep-research`** runs one research pass of a `/deep:research` loop\n593: - **`@deep-review`** runs one review pass of a `/deep:review` loop\n594: \n595: &nbsp;\n596: \n597: ## 9. 💻 COMMANDS\n598: \n599: Forty-four commands ship in six groups in the [commands folder](.skilled/commands/). Each one is a Markdown file, and most hand their steps to a YAML workflow beside it.\n600: \n601: **Spec Kit (8).** `/speckit:complete`, `/speckit:plan`, `/speckit:implement`, `/speckit:resume`, `/speckit:save`, `/speckit:search`, `/speckit:handoff` and `/speckit:ai-council`. These run the spec workflow and its continuity, as [Everyday Workflows](#5--everyday-workflows) describes.\n602: \n603: **Create (13).** `/create:sk-skill`, `/create:skill-parent`, `/create:agent`, `/create:command`, `/create:readme`, `/create:changelog`, `/create:feature-catalog`, `/create:manual-testing-playbook`, `/create:goal`, `/create:benchmark`, `/create:diff`, `/create:repo-rule` and `/create:with-human-voice`. These scaffold or revise one kind of artifact to the sk-doc standards.\n604: \n605: **Deep (2).** `/deep:research` and `/deep:review` run the autonomous loops.\n606: \n607: **Design (3).** `/design:extract` measures a live site into a style reference. `/design:chart` builds a standalone HTML chart, and `/design:diagram` draws an HTML and SVG diagram.\n608: \n609: **Prompt (1).** `/prompt:improve` turns a rough prompt into a structured one.\n610: \n611: **Doctor (17).** Health checks and repairs, listed under [Doctor Commands](#11--doctor-commands).\n612: \n613: Four runtimes add a goal command of their own, listed under the [Goal](#goal) hook.\n614: \n615: &nbsp;\n616: \n617: ## 10. 🔌 RUNTIMES AND CLI BRIDGES\n618: \n619: Skilled runs in eight AI runtimes, so you can work from the subscriptions you already have and hand work between them. Each one keeps its own folder and loads the hooks its own way:\n620: \n621: | Runtime | Folder | Commands look like | Hooks load through |\n622: | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n623: | Claude Code | `.claude/` | `/speckit:complete` | its settings file |\n624: | Codex | `.codex/` | `/speckit-complete` | its hooks file |\n625: | Cursor | `.cursor/` | `/speckit-complete` | its hooks file |\n626: | Devin | `.devin/` | skills as slash commands, such as `/system-spec-kit` | its hooks file |\n627: | OpenCode | `.opencode/` | `/speckit:complete` | one plugin per hook |\n628: | Pi | `.pi/` | `/speckit-complete` | one extension per hook |\n629: | DeepSeek Harness (DSH) | `.dsh/` | `/speckit-complete` | one guard plugin bundle |\n630: | Mistral Vibe | `.vibe/` | `/speckit-complete` | its hooks file |\n631: \n632: The eight runtimes share one source tree. Skills, agents, commands and hooks live there once, and a generator writes each runtime's copy. `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` checks that every copy still matches. Each runtime's README says which files are generated and which are authored there: [Claude Code](.claude/README.md), [Codex](.codex/README.md), [Cursor](.cursor/README.md), [Devin](.devin/README.md), [OpenCode](.opencode/README.md), [Pi](.pi/README.md) and [DeepSeek Harness](.dsh/README.md). Mistral Vibe keeps the same notes in its [sync notes](.vibe/SYNC.md).\n633: \n634: A few runtimes need one step of their own. Codex runs a repository hook only after you approve that entry, so open `/hooks` after an update and approve each entry it lists. Mistral Vibe loads its hooks only in a trusted checkout. DSH loads plugins only from the patches a run names, and a guards patch loads the guard bundle. OpenCode loads the same plugins on OpenCode 2 and OpenCode 1.\n635: \n636: Each runtime also has a bridge in the CLI orchestration hub, which [CLI Orchestration](#cli-orchestration) describes. Six bridges refuse to dispatch the runtime they run in. The Pi and DeepSeek Harness bridges may call their own runtime, but neither dispatches from inside a fan-out lineage or a dispatch that already uses it. That bound keeps delegation from looping. The DeepSeek Harness and Mistral Vibe bridges are experimental.\n637: \n638: &nbsp;\n639: \n640: ## 11. 🩺 DOCTOR COMMANDS\n641: \n642: Seventeen doctor commands check and repair the setup, one area each. Eleven belong to the `system-skilled-doctor` skill, which owns everything about Skilled inside a project. The rest sit with the skill they check, such as `/doctor:git` with sk-git. Every target that writes shows its plan and waits for your yes. `/doctor:helper` names the command that fits a problem you describe, and you can also just describe the problem in chat. The [system-skilled-doctor README](.skilled/skills/system-skilled-doctor/README.md) has the details.\n643: \n644: | Command | What it does |\n645: | --- | --- |\n646: | `/doctor:setup` | Runs the read-only setup checks and names one repair for each failing check |\n647: | `/doctor:helper` | Ranks the doctor commands against a problem in your own words |\n648: | `/doctor:install` | Prints the ordered steps that install Skilled in your own project |\n649: | `/doctor:symlink` | Checks, links or unlinks a Skilled checkout in another project |\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 650]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file README.md, lines 580-649\n580: \n581: Eleven agents own focused roles. Their source lives in the shared agents folder, which OpenCode links to. Codex, Pi, DSH and Mistral Vibe carry copies generated from it. Claude Code keeps its own hand-carried copy, and Cursor and Devin link to that copy.\n582: \n583: - **`@orchestrate`** splits multi-step work, hands each part to a specialist and merges the results\n584: - **`@code`** writes and fixes code for the detected stack and proves it works before it says done\n585: - **`@context`** finds what is already known, from packet continuity first and code search second\n586: - **`@review`** reviews code without editing it and ranks findings by severity\n587: - **`@debug`** takes a fresh look at a bug after three failed attempts, from a clean handoff\n588: - **`@markdown`** writes docs from templates and runs the `/create:*` commands\n589: - **`@prompt-improver`** turns a high-stakes prompt into a checked, structured package\n590: - **`@design`** decides visual values and builds style references, charts and diagrams\n591: - **`@ai-council`** runs several AI viewpoints toward one vetted plan and never writes code\n592: - **`@deep-research`** runs one research pass of a `/deep:research` loop\n593: - **`@deep-review`** runs one review pass of a `/deep:review` loop\n594: \n595: &nbsp;\n596: \n597: ## 9. 💻 COMMANDS\n598: \n599: Forty-four commands ship in six groups in the [commands folder](.skilled/commands/). Each one is a Markdown file, and most hand their steps to a YAML workflow beside it.\n600: \n601: **Spec Kit (8).** `/speckit:complete`, `/speckit:plan`, `/speckit:implement`, `/speckit:resume`, `/speckit:save`, `/speckit:search`, `/speckit:handoff` and `/speckit:ai-council`. These run the spec workflow and its continuity, as [Everyday Workflows](#5--everyday-workflows) describes.\n602: \n603: **Create (13).** `/create:sk-skill`, `/create:skill-parent`, `/create:agent`, `/create:command`, `/create:readme`, `/create:changelog`, `/create:feature-catalog`, `/create:manual-testing-playbook`, `/create:goal`, `/create:benchmark`, `/create:diff`, `/create:repo-rule` and `/create:with-human-voice`. These scaffold or revise one kind of artifact to the sk-doc standards.\n604: \n605: **Deep (2).** `/deep:research` and `/deep:review` run the autonomous loops.\n606: \n607: **Design (3).** `/design:extract` measures a live site into a style reference. `/design:chart` builds a standalone HTML chart, and `/design:diagram` draws an HTML and SVG diagram.\n608: \n609: **Prompt (1).** `/prompt:improve` turns a rough prompt into a structured one.\n610: \n611: **Doctor (17).** Health checks and repairs, listed under [Doctor Commands](#11--doctor-commands).\n612: \n613: Four runtimes add a goal command of their own, listed under the [Goal](#goal) hook.\n614: \n615: &nbsp;\n616: \n617: ## 10. 🔌 RUNTIMES AND CLI BRIDGES\n618: \n619: Skilled runs in eight AI runtimes, so you can work from the subscriptions you already have and hand work between them. Each one keeps its own folder and loads the hooks its own way:\n620: \n621: | Runtime | Folder | Commands look like | Hooks load through |\n622: | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n623: | Claude Code | `.claude/` | `/speckit:complete` | its settings file |\n624: | Codex | `.codex/` | `/speckit-complete` | its hooks file |\n625: | Cursor | `.cursor/` | `/speckit-complete` | its hooks file |\n626: | Devin | `.devin/` | skills as slash commands, such as `/system-spec-kit` | its hooks file |\n627: | OpenCode | `.opencode/` | `/speckit:complete` | one plugin per hook |\n628: | Pi | `.pi/` | `/speckit-complete` | one extension per hook |\n629: | DeepSeek Harness (DSH) | `.dsh/` | `/speckit-complete` | one guard plugin bundle |\n630: | Mistral Vibe | `.vibe/` | `/speckit-complete` | its hooks file |\n631: \n632: The eight runtimes share one source tree. Skills, agents, commands and hooks live there once, and a generator writes each runtime's copy. `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` checks that every copy still matches. Each runtime's README says which files are generated and which are authored there: [Claude Code](.claude/README.md), [Codex](.codex/README.md), [Cursor](.cursor/README.md), [Devin](.devin/README.md), [OpenCode](.opencode/README.md), [Pi](.pi/README.md) and [DeepSeek Harness](.dsh/README.md). Mistral Vibe keeps the same notes in its [sync notes](.vibe/SYNC.md).\n633: \n634: A few runtimes need one step of their own. Codex runs a repository hook only after you approve that entry, so open `/hooks` after an update and approve each entry it lists. Mistral Vibe loads its hooks only in a trusted checkout. DSH loads plugins only from the patches a run names, and a guards patch loads the guard bundle. OpenCode loads the same plugins on OpenCode 2 and OpenCode 1.\n635: \n636: Each runtime also has a bridge in the CLI orchestration hub, which [CLI Orchestration](#cli-orchestration) describes. Six bridges refuse to dispatch the runtime they run in. The Pi and DeepSeek Harness bridges may call their own runtime, but neither dispatches from inside a fan-out lineage or a dispatch that already uses it. That bound keeps delegation from looping. The DeepSeek Harness and Mistral Vibe bridges are experimental.\n637: \n638: &nbsp;\n639: \n640: ## 11. 🩺 DOCTOR COMMANDS\n641: \n642: Seventeen doctor commands check and repair the setup, one area each. Eleven belong to the `system-skilled-doctor` skill, which owns everything about Skilled inside a project. The rest sit with the skill they check, such as `/doctor:git` with sk-git. Every target that writes shows its plan and waits for your yes. `/doctor:helper` names the command that fits a problem you describe, and you can also just describe the problem in chat. The [system-skilled-doctor README](.skilled/skills/system-skilled-doctor/README.md) has the details.\n643: \n644: | Command | What it does |\n645: | --- | --- |\n646: | `/doctor:setup` | Runs the read-only setup checks and names one repair for each failing check |\n647: | `/doctor:helper` | Ranks the doctor commands against a problem in your own words |\n648: | `/doctor:install` | Prints the ordered steps that install Skilled in your own project |\n649: | `/doctor:symlink` | Checks, links or unlinks a Skilled checkout in another project |\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 650]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"README.md\",\"offset\":580,\"limit\":70}"},"time":{"start":1794830106211,"end":1794830107370}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794830107450,"sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeKe3TiuKUBtJoOy","part":{"partID":"prt_1e4360001001GBjbUbiJGcGhG1","sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeKe3TiuKUBtJoOy","messageID":"msg_1e435e0ed001BCd7k4RWjJCBZO","type":"tool","id":"call_81a12e1a0e2c43f1b1280f2f","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \"^name:\\|^argument-hint:\" .skilled/commands/create/*.md | head -60"},"output":".skilled/commands/create/agent.md:3:argument-hint: \"<agent_name> [agent_description] [:auto|:confirm] (:auto supports PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS: prompt-body block for non-interactive setup)\"\n.skilled/commands/create/benchmark.md:3:argument-hint: \"<skill-or-mode> <spec-packet> [create|update] --family=<family> [--benchmark-id <id>] [--date YYYY-MM-DD] [--path <dir>] [:auto|:confirm]\"\n.skilled/commands/create/changelog.md:3:argument-hint: \"<spec-folder-or-component> [--bump <major|minor|patch|build|auto>] [--release] [:auto|:confirm]\"\n.skilled/commands/create/command.md:3:argument-hint: \"<command_invocation> [command_request] [:auto|:confirm]\"\n.skilled/commands/create/diff.md:3:argument-hint: \"<target-document | --before old --after new> [--report out.html] [--view unified|side-by-side] [:auto|:confirm]\"\n.skilled/commands/create/feature-catalog.md:3:argument-hint: \"<skill-name> [create|update] [--path <dir>] [:auto|:confirm]\"\n.skilled/commands/create/goal.md:3:argument-hint: \"<packet path> [top-level|phase-parent|child|retrofit|phase-add|amend] [:auto|:confirm]\"\n.skilled/commands/create/manual-testing-playbook.md:3:argument-hint: \"<skill-name> [create|update] [--path <dir>] [:auto|:confirm]\"\n.skilled/commands/create/readme.md:3:argument-hint: \"<target> [--type <project|component|feature|skill>] [--output <path>] [:auto|:confirm]\"\n.skilled/commands/create/repo-rule.md:3:argument-hint: \"<what the rule should bind> [create|revise|retire] [--rule <name>] [:auto|:confirm]\"\n.skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md:3:argument-hint: \"<skill-name> [operation] [type] [--path <dir>] [--chained] [:auto|:confirm]\"\n.skilled/commands/create/skill-parent.md:3:argument-hint: \"<skill-name> [create|update] [--modes <mode1,mode2,...>] [--surfaces <s1,s2,...>] [--path <dir>] [:auto|:confirm]\"\n.skilled/commands/create/with-human-voice.md:3:argument-hint: \"<file or passage> [apply|score] [--include-code] [:auto|:confirm]\"\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/commands/create/agent.md:3:argument-hint: \"<agent_name> [agent_description] [:auto|:confirm] (:auto supports PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS: prompt-body block for non-interactive setup)\"\n.skilled/commands/create/benchmark.md:3:argument-hint: \"<skill-or-mode> <spec-packet> [create|update] --family=<family> [--benchmark-id <id>] [--date YYYY-MM-DD] [--path <dir>] [:auto|:confirm]\"\n.skilled/commands/create/changelog.md:3:argument-hint: \"<spec-folder-or-component> [--bump <major|minor|patch|build|auto>] [--release] [:auto|:confirm]\"\n.skilled/commands/create/command.md:3:argument-hint: \"<command_invocation> [command_request] [:auto|:confirm]\"\n.skilled/commands/create/diff.md:3:argument-hint: \"<target-document | --before old --after new> [--report out.html] [--view unified|side-by-side] [:auto|:confirm]\"\n.skilled/commands/create/feature-catalog.md:3:argument-hint: \"<skill-name> [create|update] [--path <dir>] [:auto|:confirm]\"\n.skilled/commands/create/goal.md:3:argument-hint: \"<packet path> [top-level|phase-parent|child|retrofit|phase-add|amend] [:auto|:confirm]\"\n.skilled/commands/create/manual-testing-playbook.md:3:argument-hint: \"<skill-name> [create|update] [--path <dir>] [:auto|:confirm]\"\n.skilled/commands/create/readme.md:3:argument-hint: \"<target> [--type <project|component|feature|skill>] [--output <path>] [:auto|:confirm]\"\n.skilled/commands/create/repo-rule.md:3:argument-hint: \"<what the rule should bind> [create|revise|retire] [--rule <name>] [:auto|:confirm]\"\n.skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md:3:argument-hint: \"<skill-name> [operation] [type] [--path <dir>] [--chained] [:auto|:confirm]\"\n.skilled/commands/create/skill-parent.md:3:argument-hint: \"<skill-name> [create|update] [--modes <mode1,mode2,...>] [--surfaces <s1,s2,...>] [--path <dir>] [:auto|:confirm]\"\n.skilled/commands/create/with-human-voice.md:3:argument-hint: \"<file or passage> [apply|score] [--include-code] [:auto|:confirm]\"\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \\\"^name:\\\\|^argument-hint:\\\" .skilled/commands/create/*.md | head -60\"}"},"time":{"start":1794830106625,"end":1794830107450}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794830109662,"sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeKe3TiuKUBtJoOy","part":{"id":"prt_1e4360bde001q01TihoJB3U2m1","sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeKe3TiuKUBtJoOy","messageID":"msg_1e435e0ed001BCd7k4RWjJCBZO","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"05528263d614a2c6dc32246ba283c6496cb5833a","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":1325,"output":145,"reasoning":453,"cache":{"read":72832,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794830111790,"sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeKe3TiuKUBtJoOy","part":{"id":"prt_1e436142e0015EvF1IfoLKrv44","sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeKe3TiuKUBtJoOy","messageID":"msg_1e4360be6001cADRwXPoX01QUj","type":"step-start","snapshot":"05528263d614a2c6dc32246ba283c6496cb5833a"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794830117175,"sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeKe3TiuKUBtJoOy","part":{"partID":"prt_1e4362374001nj5NZaspGW6t8C","sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeKe3TiuKUBtJoOy","messageID":"msg_1e4360be6001cADRwXPoX01QUj","type":"tool","id":"call_622be0d8aef048f99ced8564","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \"create:skill\" README.md; echo \"=== doctor table\"; sed -n 644,700p README.md"},"output":"269:Each kind also has a `/create` command for when you want the workflow directly. `/create:sk-skill` creates or updates a skill, and `/create:skill-parent` scaffolds a parent hub with its modes. `/create:agent` and `/create:command` cover agents and slash commands. `/create:readme`, `/create:changelog`, `/create:goal` and `/create:repo-rule` cover the documents around them. Every one runs with `:auto` or with `:confirm` to pause at each step.\n603:**Create (13).** `/create:sk-skill`, `/create:skill-parent`, `/create:agent`, `/create:command`, `/create:readme`, `/create:changelog`, `/create:feature-catalog`, `/create:manual-testing-playbook`, `/create:goal`, `/create:benchmark`, `/create:diff`, `/create:repo-rule` and `/create:with-human-voice`. These scaffold or revise one kind of artifact to the sk-doc standards.\n=== doctor table\n| Command | What it does |\n| --- | --- |\n| `/doctor:setup` | Runs the read-only setup checks and names one repair for each failing check |\n| `/doctor:helper` | Ranks the doctor commands against a problem in your own words |\n| `/doctor:install` | Prints the ordered steps that install Skilled in your own project |\n| `/doctor:symlink` | Checks, links or unlinks a Skilled checkout in another project |\n| `/doctor:overlay` | Checks a vendored copy's overlays, puts them back or moves the copy to a newer commit |\n| `/doctor:update` | Checks, applies or rolls back a new Skilled release |\n| `/doctor:agents-md` | Checks your root AGENTS.md against the shipped template, then embeds or restores it |\n| `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` | Checks that each runtime folder still matches the shared source |\n| `/doctor:env` | Shows every setting and where it is set, then saves a change after your yes |\n| `/doctor:mcp` | Installs, registers or debugs Code Mode |\n| `/doctor:git` | Checks the git hooks and sk-git settings, switches gates and edits the commit rules |\n| `/doctor:ci` | Lists the GitHub Actions workflows, scaffolds one or toggles a CI switch |\n| `/doctor:speckit` | Checks the trigger index, its lookup and the ripgrep recipes |\n| `/doctor:skill-advisor` | Tunes and rebuilds the skill advisor and audits its graph |\n| `/doctor:sk-skill` | Checks a skill against the Skilled format, or converts one |\n| `/doctor:sk-code` | Runs the sk-code setup checks, or checks and creates the quality config |\n| `/doctor:deep-loop` | Reads the coverage graphs and convergence of research and review runs |\n\n&nbsp;\n\n## 12. 🔗 CODE MODE MCP\n\nCode Mode lets the agent call external tools, such as Figma, GitHub, Chrome DevTools, ClickUp and Webflow, through one TypeScript interface. Tool definitions load when a call needs them, not up front, so they cost no context until then.\n\nCode Mode is the only MCP server Skilled registers. Its seven tools find tools, describe one, list them all, run a chain of calls, add or remove a provider and name the keys a tool needs. A provider config file declares 14 external providers. Their keys live in a dotenv file that only Code Mode reads.\n\n`/doctor:mcp install` builds Code Mode and registers it in seven project config files for six runtimes: OpenCode, Claude Code (two files), Codex, Cursor, Pi and Devin. Each write waits for its own approval. DSH loads Code Mode from a hand-written patch, and Mistral Vibe has no Code Mode registration. `/doctor:mcp debug` reports PASS, WARN or FAIL per check, and its fix mode adds guided repair.\n\nA call runs TypeScript against the registered tools, and one chain can call several tools in a single round trip. The [Code Mode README](.skilled/skills/mcp-code-mode/README.md) shows example calls and how each tool is named.\n\n&nbsp;\n\n## 13. 🌿 GIT WORKTREES AND LIVE SYNC\n\nEach session can work in its own git worktree, so parallel sessions never edit the same files. sk-git creates numbered worktrees and provisions them, so dependencies install and the Spec Kit builds before the first task.\n\nLive sync keeps your main checkout current. A session started through the launch wrapper publishes each commit to a shared live branch. At session start, the [live-follow](#git-live-follow) and [primary-reconcile](#git-primary-reconcile) hooks keep the main checkout on that branch.\n\nLive sync is on by default in the main checkout. One switch turns the whole loop off, and two more turn off one part each. [Off Switches](#off-switches) names the main one. The [continuous integration reference](.skilled/skills/sk-git/references/continuous-integration.md) describes the full model.\n\n&nbsp;\n\n## 14. 🔧 CONFIGURATION AND PRIVACY\n\n### Core Files\n\n[AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) holds the gates and behavior rules for every runtime. Claude Code and Codex read it directly, so there is no separate Claude instruction file. OpenCode keeps its permissions and its Code Mode binding in its own config file. Code Mode reads its providers from one provider config file.\n\n### Environment Settings\n\nEvery setting has a working default, so you can start without setting anything. The [environment example](.env.example) lists every setting the code reads, with its default and purpose. The [hook switch example](.skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env.example) lists the switches that can also live in a file.\n\nSet a value as an export in your shell profile, which wins over everything else. Or copy the hook switch example to a personal switch file beside it, which git ignores. Claude Code also reads the env block of its local settings file. `/doctor:env` shows each setting by name and never by value. It saves a change only after you approve the exact line.\n\n### Off Switches\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"269:Each kind also has a `/create` command for when you want the workflow directly. `/create:sk-skill` creates or updates a skill, and `/create:skill-parent` scaffolds a parent hub with its modes. `/create:agent` and `/create:command` cover agents and slash commands. `/create:readme`, `/create:changelog`, `/create:goal` and `/create:repo-rule` cover the documents around them. Every one runs with `:auto` or with `:confirm` to pause at each step.\n603:**Create (13).** `/create:sk-skill`, `/create:skill-parent`, `/create:agent`, `/create:command`, `/create:readme`, `/create:changelog`, `/create:feature-catalog`, `/create:manual-testing-playbook`, `/create:goal`, `/create:benchmark`, `/create:diff`, `/create:repo-rule` and `/create:with-human-voice`. These scaffold or revise one kind of artifact to the sk-doc standards.\n=== doctor table\n| Command | What it does |\n| --- | --- |\n| `/doctor:setup` | Runs the read-only setup checks and names one repair for each failing check |\n| `/doctor:helper` | Ranks the doctor commands against a problem in your own words |\n| `/doctor:install` | Prints the ordered steps that install Skilled in your own project |\n| `/doctor:symlink` | Checks, links or unlinks a Skilled checkout in another project |\n| `/doctor:overlay` | Checks a vendored copy's overlays, puts them back or moves the copy to a newer commit |\n| `/doctor:update` | Checks, applies or rolls back a new Skilled release |\n| `/doctor:agents-md` | Checks your root AGENTS.md against the shipped template, then embeds or restores it |\n| `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` | Checks that each runtime folder still matches the shared source |\n| `/doctor:env` | Shows every setting and where it is set, then saves a change after your yes |\n| `/doctor:mcp` | Installs, registers or debugs Code Mode |\n| `/doctor:git` | Checks the git hooks and sk-git settings, switches gates and edits the commit rules |\n| `/doctor:ci` | Lists the GitHub Actions workflows, scaffolds one or toggles a CI switch |\n| `/doctor:speckit` | Checks the trigger index, its lookup and the ripgrep recipes |\n| `/doctor:skill-advisor` | Tunes and rebuilds the skill advisor and audits its graph |\n| `/doctor:sk-skill` | Checks a skill against the Skilled format, or converts one |\n| `/doctor:sk-code` | Runs the sk-code setup checks, or checks and creates the quality config |\n| `/doctor:deep-loop` | Reads the coverage graphs and convergence of research and review runs |\n\n&nbsp;\n\n## 12. 🔗 CODE MODE MCP\n\nCode Mode lets the agent call external tools, such as Figma, GitHub, Chrome DevTools, ClickUp and Webflow, through one TypeScript interface. Tool definitions load when a call needs them, not up front, so they cost no context until then.\n\nCode Mode is the only MCP server Skilled registers. Its seven tools find tools, describe one, list them all, run a chain of calls, add or remove a provider and name the keys a tool needs. A provider config file declares 14 external providers. Their keys live in a dotenv file that only Code Mode reads.\n\n`/doctor:mcp install` builds Code Mode and registers it in seven project config files for six runtimes: OpenCode, Claude Code (two files), Codex, Cursor, Pi and Devin. Each write waits for its own approval. DSH loads Code Mode from a hand-written patch, and Mistral Vibe has no Code Mode registration. `/doctor:mcp debug` reports PASS, WARN or FAIL per check, and its fix mode adds guided repair.\n\nA call runs TypeScript against the registered tools, and one chain can call several tools in a single round trip. The [Code Mode README](.skilled/skills/mcp-code-mode/README.md) shows example calls and how each tool is named.\n\n&nbsp;\n\n## 13. 🌿 GIT WORKTREES AND LIVE SYNC\n\nEach session can work in its own git worktree, so parallel sessions never edit the same files. sk-git creates numbered worktrees and provisions them, so dependencies install and the Spec Kit builds before the first task.\n\nLive sync keeps your main checkout current. A session started through the launch wrapper publishes each commit to a shared live branch. At session start, the [live-follow](#git-live-follow) and [primary-reconcile](#git-primary-reconcile) hooks keep the main checkout on that branch.\n\nLive sync is on by default in the main checkout. One switch turns the whole loop off, and two more turn off one part each. [Off Switches](#off-switches) names the main one. The [continuous integration reference](.skilled/skills/sk-git/references/continuous-integration.md) describes the full model.\n\n&nbsp;\n\n## 14. 🔧 CONFIGURATION AND PRIVACY\n\n### Core Files\n\n[AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) holds the gates and behavior rules for every runtime. Claude Code and Codex read it directly, so there is no separate Claude instruction file. OpenCode keeps its permissions and its Code Mode binding in its own config file. Code Mode reads its providers from one provider config file.\n\n### Environment Settings\n\nEvery setting has a working default, so you can start without setting anything. The [environment example](.env.example) lists every setting the code reads, with its default and purpose. The [hook switch example](.skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env.example) lists the switches that can also live in a file.\n\nSet a value as an export in your shell profile, which wins over everything else. Or copy the hook switch example to a personal switch file beside it, which git ignores. Claude Code also reads the env block of its local settings file. `/doctor:env` shows each setting by name and never by value. It saves a change only after you approve the exact line.\n\n### Off Switches\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \\\"create:skill\\\" README.md; echo \\\"=== doctor table\\\"; sed -n 644,700p README.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794830115700,"end":1794830117175}}}}
