{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794830137947,"sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeKe3TiuKUBtJoOy","part":{"partID":"prt_1e4367522002cB8Vg5HtERHVlf","sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeKe3TiuKUBtJoOy","messageID":"msg_1e4362da6001Ap2ZdgfL5c14hw","type":"tool","id":"call_30de62da83bb4df6ad2cae1b","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n 1,40p .skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md"},"output":"---\ndescription: Create or update OpenCode skills via one unified command with operation routing. :auto/:confirm.\nargument-hint: \"<skill-name> [operation] [type] [--path <dir>] [--chained] [:auto|:confirm]\"\nallowed-tools: Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Glob, Grep, TodoWrite\n---\n\n# /create:sk-skill Router\n\nThis command is a thin router. It separates execution routing from user-facing presentation.\n\n## 1. ROUTER CONTRACT\n\nRoute /create:sk-skill to its presentation contract and workflow YAML for creating or updating OpenCode skills through the unified skill command.\n\n- Do not split behavior across legacy command definitions.\n- Do not edit workflow YAML while executing this command.\n\n---\n\n## 2. OWNED ASSETS\n\n| Purpose | Asset |\n|---------|-------|\n| Presentation contract | `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt` |\n| Auto workflow | `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-auto.yaml` |\n| Confirm workflow | `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-confirm.yaml` |\n\n---\n\n## 3. MODE ROUTING\n\n- If any referenced asset is missing, stop and report the missing path.\n- The YAML owns workflow behavior; the presentation Markdown owns user-visible wording and layout.\n\n1. Read `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt`.\n2. Run the presentation contract's Phase 0 verification and setup resolution.\n3. Resolve operation from setup: `full-create`, `full-update`, `reference-only`, or `asset-only`.\n4. Resolve execution mode from `$ARGUMENTS` or the setup answer: `:auto` or `:confirm`.\n5. Load the workflow YAML bound to the resolved mode from the EXECUTION TARGETS table below.\n6. Execute the selected YAML step by step and route to the resolved operation branch.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\ndescription: Create or update OpenCode skills via one unified command with operation routing. :auto/:confirm.\nargument-hint: \"<skill-name> [operation] [type] [--path <dir>] [--chained] [:auto|:confirm]\"\nallowed-tools: Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Glob, Grep, TodoWrite\n---\n\n# /create:sk-skill Router\n\nThis command is a thin router. It separates execution routing from user-facing presentation.\n\n## 1. ROUTER CONTRACT\n\nRoute /create:sk-skill to its presentation contract and workflow YAML for creating or updating OpenCode skills through the unified skill command.\n\n- Do not split behavior across legacy command definitions.\n- Do not edit workflow YAML while executing this command.\n\n---\n\n## 2. OWNED ASSETS\n\n| Purpose | Asset |\n|---------|-------|\n| Presentation contract | `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt` |\n| Auto workflow | `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-auto.yaml` |\n| Confirm workflow | `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-confirm.yaml` |\n\n---\n\n## 3. MODE ROUTING\n\n- If any referenced asset is missing, stop and report the missing path.\n- The YAML owns workflow behavior; the presentation Markdown owns user-visible wording and layout.\n\n1. Read `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt`.\n2. Run the presentation contract's Phase 0 verification and setup resolution.\n3. Resolve operation from setup: `full-create`, `full-update`, `reference-only`, or `asset-only`.\n4. Resolve execution mode from `$ARGUMENTS` or the setup answer: `:auto` or `:confirm`.\n5. Load the workflow YAML bound to the resolved mode from the EXECUTION TARGETS table below.\n6. Execute the selected YAML step by step and route to the resolved operation branch.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n 1,40p .skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794830136610,"end":1794830137947}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794830137962,"sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeKe3TiuKUBtJoOy","part":{"partID":"prt_1e4367734001YszuaUsK7VHIop","sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeKe3TiuKUBtJoOy","messageID":"msg_1e4362da6001Ap2ZdgfL5c14hw","type":"tool","id":"call_c7d6699c380d40d8ba6012e9","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && for d in .opencode .claude .codex .cursor .devin .pi .dsh .vibe; do echo \"== $d\"; ls $d/commands/create 2>/dev/null | grep -i skill; done"},"output":"== .opencode\nsk-skill.md\nskill-parent.md\n== .claude\nsk-skill.md\nskill-parent.md\n== .codex\n== .cursor\n== .devin\n== .pi\n== .dsh\n== .vibe\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":1},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"== .opencode\nsk-skill.md\nskill-parent.md\n== .claude\nsk-skill.md\nskill-parent.md\n== .codex\n== .cursor\n== .devin\n== .pi\n== .dsh\n== .vibe\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Exit code: 1"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && for d in .opencode .claude .codex .cursor .devin .pi .dsh .vibe; do echo \\\"== $d\\\"; ls $d/commands/create 2>/dev/null | grep -i skill; done\"}"},"time":{"start":1794830137140,"end":1794830137962}}}}
