{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794830169110,"sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeKe3TiuKUBtJoOy","part":{"partID":"prt_1e436efe2001SJpujk4YP5C9nu","sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeKe3TiuKUBtJoOy","messageID":"msg_1e436d377001sdDZARtIzaMhKX","type":"tool","id":"call_55ea5409b5ef4c37870761bc","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \"create:sk-skill\\|create:skill-parent\\|create a skill\\|new skill\\|skill command\" README.md | head -30"},"output":"267:Extending Skilled follows the same framework that built it. The [sk-doc](.skilled/skills/sk-doc/README.md) hub holds a template, a set of standards and a validator for each kind of component. Ask for a new skill, agent or command in plain words and the advisor loads the matching sk-doc mode, so the result matches the rest of the repository.\n269:Each kind also has a `/create` command for when you want the workflow directly. `/create:sk-skill` creates or updates a skill, and `/create:skill-parent` scaffolds a parent hub with its modes. `/create:agent` and `/create:command` cover agents and slash commands. `/create:readme`, `/create:changelog`, `/create:goal` and `/create:repo-rule` cover the documents around them. Every one runs with `:auto` or with `:confirm` to pause at each step.\n271:Updating works the same way as creating. Name the component and the change, and the workflow edits it in place, checks it against its template and runs the sk-doc validator. A new skill needs no registration step, because the advisor finds it from its own metadata.\n603:**Create (13).** `/create:sk-skill`, `/create:skill-parent`, `/create:agent`, `/create:command`, `/create:readme`, `/create:changelog`, `/create:feature-catalog`, `/create:manual-testing-playbook`, `/create:goal`, `/create:benchmark`, `/create:diff`, `/create:repo-rule` and `/create:with-human-voice`. These scaffold or revise one kind of artifact to the sk-doc standards.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"267:Extending Skilled follows the same framework that built it. The [sk-doc](.skilled/skills/sk-doc/README.md) hub holds a template, a set of standards and a validator for each kind of component. Ask for a new skill, agent or command in plain words and the advisor loads the matching sk-doc mode, so the result matches the rest of the repository.\n269:Each kind also has a `/create` command for when you want the workflow directly. `/create:sk-skill` creates or updates a skill, and `/create:skill-parent` scaffolds a parent hub with its modes. `/create:agent` and `/create:command` cover agents and slash commands. `/create:readme`, `/create:changelog`, `/create:goal` and `/create:repo-rule` cover the documents around them. Every one runs with `:auto` or with `:confirm` to pause at each step.\n271:Updating works the same way as creating. Name the component and the change, and the workflow edits it in place, checks it against its template and runs the sk-doc validator. A new skill needs no registration step, because the advisor finds it from its own metadata.\n603:**Create (13).** `/create:sk-skill`, `/create:skill-parent`, `/create:agent`, `/create:command`, `/create:readme`, `/create:changelog`, `/create:feature-catalog`, `/create:manual-testing-playbook`, `/create:goal`, `/create:benchmark`, `/create:diff`, `/create:repo-rule` and `/create:with-human-voice`. These scaffold or revise one kind of artifact to the sk-doc standards.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \\\"create:sk-skill\\\\|create:skill-parent\\\\|create a skill\\\\|new skill\\\\|skill command\\\" README.md | head -30\"}"},"time":{"start":1794830168034,"end":1794830169110}}}}
