{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794830200758,"sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeKe3TiuKUBtJoOy","part":{"partID":"prt_1e4376c70001F54HHoJQTUaCYU","sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeKe3TiuKUBtJoOy","messageID":"msg_1e43736c0001vrSuA2r3cxC7gL","type":"tool","id":"call_bd973e0f4d8741efbcf06dc4","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && head -12 .skilled/commands/doctor/sk-skill.md; echo \"=== create README.txt\"; sed -n 1,40p .skilled/commands/create/README.txt"},"output":"---\ndescription: \"Check a skill against the Skilled format, or convert one to it, plan first.\"\nargument-hint: \"[check|convert] [<name-or-path>] [--json] [--into-hub <hub>] [--dry-run]\"\nallowed-tools: Read, Bash\n---\n<!-- skill_agent: sk-doc -->\n\n# /doctor:sk-skill Router\n\nThis command is a thin router. It binds the read-only `check` target or the mutating `convert` target from `_routes.yaml`, then loads that target's workflow YAML and the presentation contract.\n\n## 1. ROUTER CONTRACT\n=== create README.txt\n---\ntitle: \"Create Commands\"\ndescription: \"Slash commands for scaffolding OpenCode components, docs, changelogs, charts, diagrams, diffs and repo rules.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"create command\"\n  - \"scaffold component\"\n  - \"create agent\"\n  - \"create skill\"\n  - \"create readme\"\n  - \"create feature catalog\"\n  - \"create testing playbook\"\n  - \"create changelog\"\n  - \"create chart\"\n  - \"create diagram\"\n  - \"create diff\"\n  - \"create repo rule\"\n  - \"apply human voice\"\n---\n\n# Create Commands\n\n> Slash commands for scaffolding OpenCode components, documentation packages, changelog entries, charts, diagrams, diff reports and repo rules with proper templates and validation.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nThe `create` command group scaffolds OpenCode components, documentation packages, changelog entries, and standalone visual and prose artifacts. All commands follow a structured YAML workflow and support `:auto` (no approval prompts) and `:confirm` (pause at each step) execution modes.\n\nThe table in section 3 lists every command in this folder. When a command file is added here, add its row there too; a missing row is the failure mode this index has hit before.\n\nAll shipped `create` commands run Phase 0 (@markdown agent self-verification).\n\n---\n\n## 2. PURPOSE\n\nUse this index to understand which `/create:*` command owns a given scaffolding workflow, which argument shape it expects, and which package contract or artifact family it generates.\n\nThis document is a routing and reference surface only. Run the command entrypoint itself for execution, setup prompting, and YAML workflow dispatch.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\ndescription: \"Check a skill against the Skilled format, or convert one to it, plan first.\"\nargument-hint: \"[check|convert] [<name-or-path>] [--json] [--into-hub <hub>] [--dry-run]\"\nallowed-tools: Read, Bash\n---\n<!-- skill_agent: sk-doc -->\n\n# /doctor:sk-skill Router\n\nThis command is a thin router. It binds the read-only `check` target or the mutating `convert` target from `_routes.yaml`, then loads that target's workflow YAML and the presentation contract.\n\n## 1. ROUTER CONTRACT\n=== create README.txt\n---\ntitle: \"Create Commands\"\ndescription: \"Slash commands for scaffolding OpenCode components, docs, changelogs, charts, diagrams, diffs and repo rules.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"create command\"\n  - \"scaffold component\"\n  - \"create agent\"\n  - \"create skill\"\n  - \"create readme\"\n  - \"create feature catalog\"\n  - \"create testing playbook\"\n  - \"create changelog\"\n  - \"create chart\"\n  - \"create diagram\"\n  - \"create diff\"\n  - \"create repo rule\"\n  - \"apply human voice\"\n---\n\n# Create Commands\n\n> Slash commands for scaffolding OpenCode components, documentation packages, changelog entries, charts, diagrams, diff reports and repo rules with proper templates and validation.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nThe `create` command group scaffolds OpenCode components, documentation packages, changelog entries, and standalone visual and prose artifacts. All commands follow a structured YAML workflow and support `:auto` (no approval prompts) and `:confirm` (pause at each step) execution modes.\n\nThe table in section 3 lists every command in this folder. When a command file is added here, add its row there too; a missing row is the failure mode this index has hit before.\n\nAll shipped `create` commands run Phase 0 (@markdown agent self-verification).\n\n---\n\n## 2. PURPOSE\n\nUse this index to understand which `/create:*` command owns a given scaffolding workflow, which argument shape it expects, and which package contract or artifact family it generates.\n\nThis document is a routing and reference surface only. Run the command entrypoint itself for execution, setup prompting, and YAML workflow dispatch.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && head -12 .skilled/commands/doctor/sk-skill.md; echo \\\"=== create README.txt\\\"; sed -n 1,40p .skilled/commands/create/README.txt\"}"},"time":{"start":1794830199920,"end":1794830200758}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794830200767,"sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeKe3TiuKUBtJoOy","part":{"partID":"prt_1e4376995001N4FUwgz17WAeRy","sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeKe3TiuKUBtJoOy","messageID":"msg_1e43736c0001vrSuA2r3cxC7gL","type":"tool","id":"call_37ef68f7cfc448b78e89f5e3","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n 1,25p .skilled/commands/local-skilled-alignment.md; echo \"=== README.txt\"; sed -n 1,40p .skilled/commands/README.txt"},"output":"---\ndescription: \"Check a .skilled change against every connected surface and write a findings report. Modes :auto, :confirm.\"\nargument-hint: \"[target] [:auto|:confirm] [--surfaces=S1,S2] [--base=REF] [--out=DIR] [--config=PATH] [--no-lanes] [--recheck=RUN_DIR] [--fix=literal] [--lanes=NAME] [--keep=N]\"\nallowed-tools: Read, Write, Bash, Grep, Glob, Task\n---\n\n# Local Skilled Alignment\n\nThin router for the operator-local alignment check. It resolves the target and execution mode, loads the presentation contract, then executes the owned workflow YAML.\n\n## 1. ROUTER CONTRACT\n\nDo not dispatch agents or write artifacts from this Markdown file. Review-lane dispatch, the critic dispatch and every artifact write are owned by the workflow YAML. Load the presentation contract before showing any setup prompt, checkpoint, result or next-step text.\n\nThe run is report-only unless `--fix literal` is passed, which applies only exact literal fixes the critic did not overturn. It never stages, commits or pushes, and otherwise writes only under its output folder, which sits outside the checkout.\n\n---\n\n## 2. OWNED ASSETS\n\n| Purpose | Asset |\n|---------|-------|\n| Presentation source of truth | `.skilled/commands/assets/local-skilled-alignment/local-skilled-alignment-presentation.txt` |\n| Auto workflow | `.skilled/commands/assets/local-skilled-alignment/local-skilled-alignment-auto.yaml` |\n| Confirm workflow | `.skilled/commands/assets/local-skilled-alignment/local-skilled-alignment-confirm.yaml` |\n=== README.txt\n---\ntitle: \"OpenCode Commands\"\ndescription: \"OpenCode slash commands: component creation, deep loops, prompts, continuity and spec kit workflows.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"opencode commands\"\n  - \"slash commands\"\n  - \"command reference\"\n  - \"available commands\"\n---\n\n# OpenCode Commands\n\n> Slash commands that provide structured workflows for component creation, deep loops, prompt improvement, packet continuity, and spec kit operations.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nCommands are invoked as slash commands (e.g., `/create:feature-catalog`, `/deep:review`, `/prompt:improve`, `/speckit:save`, `/speckit:plan`). Each command is a markdown file with YAML frontmatter that defines its description, argument hints, and allowed tools.\n\nCommands are organized into six groups:\n\n| Group | Path | Commands | Purpose |\n|-------|------|----------|---------|\n| **create** | `commands/create/` | 13 | Scaffold OpenCode components, documentation packages, changelogs, charts, diagrams, diffs and repo rules |\n| **deep** | `commands/deep/` | 2 | Deep research and review loops |\n| **doctor** | `commands/doctor/` | 17 | Setup overview, problem-to-command routing, spec-kit retrieval, skill advisor, deep-loop, runtime-mirror, sk-code setup, CI workflow switches, skill format check, git hook and standards, MCP, release-update, project-repo symlink check, link and unlink, ordered install guide, vendored-tree overlay status, apply and re-pin, root instruction-file check and embed, and environment-switch diagnostics |\n| **design** | `commands/design/` | 3 | Style Reference extraction, standalone charts and diagrams |\n| **prompt** | `commands/prompt/` | 1 | Prompt engineering surface (`/prompt:improve`) via sk-prompt |\n| **speckit** | `commands/speckit/` | 8 | Spec folder workflows (plan, implement, resume and complete), context save (save), lexical search (search), the manual trigger for the session handover loop (handoff) and a single-round AI council (ai-council) |\n\nOne OpenCode-only command lives outside this tree: `/goal-opencode` manages the passive session goal via the `opencode-goal` plugin, so it is authored in `.opencode/commands/goal-opencode.md`, beside that directory's links to these groups. The prompt-improvement surface lives in the `prompt` group as `prompt/improve.md` (invoked `/prompt:improve`).\n\nEach group's command count above is the number of command files in that folder. When a command is added, update the count and its row in section 4. A group whose file set outgrew this index is the failure mode this document has hit before.\n\n---\n\n## 2. PURPOSE\n\nUse this document as the top-level routing reference for the OpenCode slash-command surface. It explains which command group owns which workflow and points readers to the canonical sub-index for deeper command-family detail.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\ndescription: \"Check a .skilled change against every connected surface and write a findings report. Modes :auto, :confirm.\"\nargument-hint: \"[target] [:auto|:confirm] [--surfaces=S1,S2] [--base=REF] [--out=DIR] [--config=PATH] [--no-lanes] [--recheck=RUN_DIR] [--fix=literal] [--lanes=NAME] [--keep=N]\"\nallowed-tools: Read, Write, Bash, Grep, Glob, Task\n---\n\n# Local Skilled Alignment\n\nThin router for the operator-local alignment check. It resolves the target and execution mode, loads the presentation contract, then executes the owned workflow YAML.\n\n## 1. ROUTER CONTRACT\n\nDo not dispatch agents or write artifacts from this Markdown file. Review-lane dispatch, the critic dispatch and every artifact write are owned by the workflow YAML. Load the presentation contract before showing any setup prompt, checkpoint, result or next-step text.\n\nThe run is report-only unless `--fix literal` is passed, which applies only exact literal fixes the critic did not overturn. It never stages, commits or pushes, and otherwise writes only under its output folder, which sits outside the checkout.\n\n---\n\n## 2. OWNED ASSETS\n\n| Purpose | Asset |\n|---------|-------|\n| Presentation source of truth | `.skilled/commands/assets/local-skilled-alignment/local-skilled-alignment-presentation.txt` |\n| Auto workflow | `.skilled/commands/assets/local-skilled-alignment/local-skilled-alignment-auto.yaml` |\n| Confirm workflow | `.skilled/commands/assets/local-skilled-alignment/local-skilled-alignment-confirm.yaml` |\n=== README.txt\n---\ntitle: \"OpenCode Commands\"\ndescription: \"OpenCode slash commands: component creation, deep loops, prompts, continuity and spec kit workflows.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"opencode commands\"\n  - \"slash commands\"\n  - \"command reference\"\n  - \"available commands\"\n---\n\n# OpenCode Commands\n\n> Slash commands that provide structured workflows for component creation, deep loops, prompt improvement, packet continuity, and spec kit operations.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nCommands are invoked as slash commands (e.g., `/create:feature-catalog`, `/deep:review`, `/prompt:improve`, `/speckit:save`, `/speckit:plan`). Each command is a markdown file with YAML frontmatter that defines its description, argument hints, and allowed tools.\n\nCommands are organized into six groups:\n\n| Group | Path | Commands | Purpose |\n|-------|------|----------|---------|\n| **create** | `commands/create/` | 13 | Scaffold OpenCode components, documentation packages, changelogs, charts, diagrams, diffs and repo rules |\n| **deep** | `commands/deep/` | 2 | Deep research and review loops |\n| **doctor** | `commands/doctor/` | 17 | Setup overview, problem-to-command routing, spec-kit retrieval, skill advisor, deep-loop, runtime-mirror, sk-code setup, CI workflow switches, skill format check, git hook and standards, MCP, release-update, project-repo symlink check, link and unlink, ordered install guide, vendored-tree overlay status, apply and re-pin, root instruction-file check and embed, and environment-switch diagnostics |\n| **design** | `commands/design/` | 3 | Style Reference extraction, standalone charts and diagrams |\n| **prompt** | `commands/prompt/` | 1 | Prompt engineering surface (`/prompt:improve`) via sk-prompt |\n| **speckit** | `commands/speckit/` | 8 | Spec folder workflows (plan, implement, resume and complete), context save (save), lexical search (search), the manual trigger for the session handover loop (handoff) and a single-round AI council (ai-council) |\n\nOne OpenCode-only command lives outside this tree: `/goal-opencode` manages the passive session goal via the `opencode-goal` plugin, so it is authored in `.opencode/commands/goal-opencode.md`, beside that directory's links to these groups. The prompt-improvement surface lives in the `prompt` group as `prompt/improve.md` (invoked `/prompt:improve`).\n\nEach group's command count above is the number of command files in that folder. When a command is added, update the count and its row in section 4. A group whose file set outgrew this index is the failure mode this document has hit before.\n\n---\n\n## 2. PURPOSE\n\nUse this document as the top-level routing reference for the OpenCode slash-command surface. It explains which command group owns which workflow and points readers to the canonical sub-index for deeper command-family detail.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n 1,25p .skilled/commands/local-skilled-alignment.md; echo \\\"=== README.txt\\\"; sed -n 1,40p .skilled/commands/README.txt\"}"},"time":{"start":1794830199189,"end":1794830200767}}}}
