{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794830227054,"sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeKe3TiuKUBtJoOy","part":{"partID":"prt_1e437d4de001SUuYBM3xciEb1y","sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeKe3TiuKUBtJoOy","messageID":"msg_1e437a26a001iRKozy0lJojMGf","type":"tool","id":"call_00_roulmvo1hcn4mkfz01waed3p","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && ls .opencode/commands/goal-opencode.md .cursor/commands/goal-cursor.md .pi/commands/goal-pi.md .dsh/commands/goal-dsh.md 2>&1; echo \"=== grep goal commands in README\"; grep -n \"goal-opencode\\|goal-cursor\\|goal-pi\\|goal-dsh\" README.md"},"output":"ls: .dsh/commands/goal-dsh.md: No such file or directory\nls: .pi/commands/goal-pi.md: No such file or directory\n.cursor/commands/goal-cursor.md\n.opencode/commands/goal-opencode.md\n=== grep goal commands in README\n341:A spec folder can hold a goal file with the directive and the criteria that decide when the work is done. This hook binds a session to that file and injects a short slice of it, so the goal survives context resets. `/create:goal` writes the file. Claude Code and Codex use their own `/goal` command instead, and the spec workflows hand you the slice to paste. OpenCode manages the goal with `/goal-opencode`, Pi with `/goal-pi` and DSH with `/goal-dsh`. Cursor's `/goal-cursor` can only read a packet's goal.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"ls: .dsh/commands/goal-dsh.md: No such file or directory\nls: .pi/commands/goal-pi.md: No such file or directory\n.cursor/commands/goal-cursor.md\n.opencode/commands/goal-opencode.md\n=== grep goal commands in README\n341:A spec folder can hold a goal file with the directive and the criteria that decide when the work is done. This hook binds a session to that file and injects a short slice of it, so the goal survives context resets. `/create:goal` writes the file. Claude Code and Codex use their own `/goal` command instead, and the spec workflows hand you the slice to paste. OpenCode manages the goal with `/goal-opencode`, Pi with `/goal-pi` and DSH with `/goal-dsh`. Cursor's `/goal-cursor` can only read a packet's goal.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && ls .opencode/commands/goal-opencode.md .cursor/commands/goal-cursor.md .pi/commands/goal-pi.md .dsh/commands/goal-dsh.md 2>&1; echo \\\"=== grep goal commands in README\\\"; grep -n \\\"goal-opencode\\\\|goal-cursor\\\\|goal-pi\\\\|goal-dsh\\\" README.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794830226654,"end":1794830227054}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794830227092,"sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeKe3TiuKUBtJoOy","part":{"partID":"prt_1e437d5340011yfThVYu9PVk2g","sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeKe3TiuKUBtJoOy","messageID":"msg_1e437a26a001iRKozy0lJojMGf","type":"tool","id":"call_01_129nxwm7iad3xpvo4s7w2cvr","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -c \"^\" README.md && git show origin/main:README.md | grep -n \"Forty-four commands\\|Create (13)\\|create:skill\" | head"},"output":"779\n269:Each kind also has a `/create` command for when you want the workflow directly. `/create:skill` creates or updates a skill, and `/create:skill-parent` scaffolds a parent hub with its modes. `/create:agent` and `/create:command` cover agents and slash commands. `/create:readme`, `/create:changelog`, `/create:goal` and `/create:repo-rule` cover the documents around them. Every one runs with `:auto` or with `:confirm` to pause at each step.\n599:Forty-four commands ship in six groups in the [commands folder](.skilled/commands/). Each one is a Markdown file, and most hand their steps to a YAML workflow beside it.\n603:**Create (13).** `/create:skill`, `/create:skill-parent`, `/create:agent`, `/create:command`, `/create:readme`, `/create:changelog`, `/create:feature-catalog`, `/create:manual-testing-playbook`, `/create:goal`, `/create:benchmark`, `/create:diff`, `/create:repo-rule` and `/create:with-human-voice`. These scaffold or revise one kind of artifact to the sk-doc standards.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"779\n269:Each kind also has a `/create` command for when you want the workflow directly. `/create:skill` creates or updates a skill, and `/create:skill-parent` scaffolds a parent hub with its modes. `/create:agent` and `/create:command` cover agents and slash commands. `/create:readme`, `/create:changelog`, `/create:goal` and `/create:repo-rule` cover the documents around them. Every one runs with `:auto` or with `:confirm` to pause at each step.\n599:Forty-four commands ship in six groups in the [commands folder](.skilled/commands/). Each one is a Markdown file, and most hand their steps to a YAML workflow beside it.\n603:**Create (13).** `/create:skill`, `/create:skill-parent`, `/create:agent`, `/create:command`, `/create:readme`, `/create:changelog`, `/create:feature-catalog`, `/create:manual-testing-playbook`, `/create:goal`, `/create:benchmark`, `/create:diff`, `/create:repo-rule` and `/create:with-human-voice`. These scaffold or revise one kind of artifact to the sk-doc standards.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -c \\\"^\\\" README.md && git show origin/main:README.md | grep -n \\\"Forty-four commands\\\\|Create (13)\\\\|create:skill\\\" | head\"}"},"time":{"start":1794830226740,"end":1794830227092}}}}
