_package.py [skill_path]/[skill_name] --strict . This is the authoritative structural gate (hard-fails missing/non-4-part version, name!=folder, or missing required sections). It MUST pass before completion, and the generated tree must contain no non-exempt underscore path segment.\"\n458:      - \"Run python3 .skilled/skills/sk-doc/scripts/package_skill.py [skill_path]/[skill_name] --check --strict. The strict completion gate runs that check and rejects the old routing shape (RS-001 to RS-005): a SMART ROUTING section over 12 lines or 180 words, a '## MACHINE ROUTER' section left in SKILL.md, that section not last, a missing sibling ROUTER.md or one whose real path leaves the skill folder, and a SKILL.md with no relative link to ./ROUTER.md.\"\n464:    gate:\n545:      Mode: :confirm\n566:      - Memory saved: [yes/no]\n623:  message: \"Unified sk-skill confirm workflow complete.\"\n626:      action: \"/create:sk-skill [skill-name] full-update :confirm\"\n628:      action: \"/create:sk-skill [skill-name] reference-only [type] :confirm\"\n630:      action: \"/create:sk-skill [skill-name] asset-only [type] :confirm\"\n647:    - \"Bypass hard gates\"\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"11:action: Route one operation branch with user checkpoints, hard gates, and validation loops\n30:  approvals: step_by_step\n39:    Executes the 7-step skill creation workflow with approval gates at each checkpoint.\n40:    User confirms, reviews, or modifies at each step before the workflow advances.\n65:    action: \"Return to setup gate or current step with explicit correction options\"\n85:      - \"execution_mode is :confirm\"\n159:  execution_mode: :confirm\n258:gate_logic:\n272:    H4_validation_gate:\n275:    H4b_human_voice_gate:\n320:      - Validate execution_mode is :confirm\n386:          - \"Run node .skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/generate-leaf-manifest.cjs --check [skill_root] to report leaf-manifest.json freshness (fresh|stale|missing) for the completion handoff. This is a read-only drift check, not regeneration — full-update never ran the class-metadata gate, so unlike full-create it cannot assume freshness and must measure it\"\n437:      - Read `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-with-human-voice/SKILL.md` and follow its score operation, scope gate, mechanical scan, judgment pass, scoring rules, and report shape\n443:      - Record each target's scan output and exit code, confirmed blockers, score or length basis, judgment findings, exceptions, and verdict for the presentation\n449:    gate:\n457:      - \"Run the completion gate: python3 .skilled/skills/sk-doc/scripts/validate_skill_package.py [skill_path]/[skill_name] --strict . This is the authoritative structural gate (hard-fails missing/non-4-part version, name!=folder, or missing required sections). It MUST pass before completion, and the generated tree must contain no non-exempt underscore path segment.\"\n458:      - \"Run python3 .skilled/skills/sk-doc/scripts/package_skill.py [skill_path]/[skill_name] --check --strict. The strict completion gate runs that check and rejects the old routing shape (RS-001 to RS-005): a SMART ROUTING section over 12 lines or 180 words, a '## MACHINE ROUTER' section left in SKILL.md, that section not last, a missing sibling ROUTER.md or one whose real path leaves the skill folder, and a SKILL.md with no relative link to ./ROUTER.md.\"\n464:    gate:\n545:      Mode: :confirm\n566:      - Memory saved: [yes/no]\n623:  message: \"Unified sk-skill confirm workflow complete.\"\n626:      action: \"/create:sk-skill [skill-name] full-update :confirm\"\n628:      action: \"/create:sk-skill [skill-name] reference-only [type] :confirm\"\n630:      action: \"/create:sk-skill [skill-name] asset-only [type] :confirm\"\n647:    - \"Bypass hard gates\"\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": 