{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794830419001,"sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeKe3TiuKUBtJoOy","part":{"partID":"prt_1e43ac0a80012HBhimF91i3hgD","sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeKe3TiuKUBtJoOy","messageID":"msg_1e43a7ad2001XCNTUFmEv41Rd3","type":"tool","id":"call_00_esnp03anfgip72cjgflczx1o","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 001\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Lineage: `docs-7`, area `docs`.\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder).\n- Focus: traceability, with correctness, security and maintainability lenses applied to the same two changed README lines. The pass-seven operator focus is the docs area: this branch's net change to the root `README.md` against `origin/main`, where `/create:skill` was renamed `/create:sk-skill`, so every command name the README gives is checked against `.skilled/commands`. `review/review-brief-7.txt` and `review/review-scope-7.txt` were read first; this iteration covers the area they assign to `docs-7`.\n- Diff base: `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff origin/main 1c3d62def5a -- README.md`, the command on line 1 of the scope file. It reports two lines changed, 2 insertions and 2 deletions: `README.md:269` and `README.md:603`.\n- `steer.md` does not exist in the lineage directory, so no lead ruling applied.\n- Recorded limits and the holdout rule were honoured: no prompt corpus was opened, no `git diff`/`show`/`log -p` ran over a path containing one, `score-command-transcripts.mjs --summary` was not run, and no CLI session store was read.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n| File | Lines read | What was checked |\n|------|-----------|------------------|\n| `README.md` | 266-271 | The changed extending-Skilled paragraph: the renamed `/create:sk-skill` and the remaining `/create:*` names, plus the `:auto`/`:confirm` sentence |\n| `README.md` | 580-613 | The agent list and the whole commands section: all 44 names, the six group counts, and the changed Create list |\n| `README.md` | 640-663 | The Doctor table, to test the `Doctor (17)` count against real files |\n| `README.md` | 341 | The runtime goal-command paragraph, to confirm the four runtime-owned goal commands are outside the 44 |\n| `.skilled/commands/README.txt` | 1-40 | The command tree's own six-group index and counts |\n| `.skilled/commands/create/README.txt` | 50-95, 119-180 | The create group index rows, the command-map tree, and every example invocation of the renamed command |\n| `.skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md` | 1-40 | The renamed router's frontmatter name, description, argument hint and owned assets |\n| `.skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md` | 40-80 | The mode routing and execution targets for `:auto` and `:confirm` |\n| `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/README.md` | 60-70, 190-198 | The sk-doc hub's thirteen-command sentence and its how-do-I answer naming `/create:sk-skill` |\n\nContext evidence (read-only, outside the docs scope path): `.skilled/commands/**` file inventory, `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt:1,28`, `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-auto.yaml:113`, `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-confirm.yaml:30,39-40`, `.opencode/commands/create/sk-skill.md`, `.claude/commands/create/sk-skill.md`.\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\n|----------|--------|----------|\n| `spec_code` | pass | Both changed lines name a command file that exists: `/create:sk-skill` resolves to `.skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md` and every other `/group:name` token in `README.md` resolves to `.skilled/commands/<group>/<name>.md` (44 of 44). The two changed lines agree with each other. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | notApplicable | The review target has no `checklist.md` at the packet root; the pass-seven brief and scope file are the operative checklist and both were read. |\n| `skill_agent` | pass | The renamed command's own surfaces agree with the README name: `.skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md:1-13` routes `/create:sk-skill`, and `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt:1,28` presents the same name. |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | notApplicable | No agent body is in the docs scope; the command mirrors that do exist are recorded under Integration Evidence. |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | notApplicable | No feature-catalog claim is touched by the two changed README lines. |\n| `playbook_capability` | notApplicable | No manual-testing-playbook claim is touched by the two changed README lines. |\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- `.skilled/commands/README.txt:21-35` gives the six-group table: create 13, deep 2, doctor 17, design 3, prompt 1, speckit 8, which sums to the README's `Forty-four commands ship in six groups` at `README.md:599`; `local-skilled-alignment.md` sits at the tree root and is not counted in the six groups.\n- `.skilled/commands/create/README.txt:57` names `/create:sk-skill <skill-name> [operation] [type] [--path <dir>] [--chained] [:auto|:confirm]`, and `:88` maps `sk-skill.md` to `/create:sk-skill`; both agree with `README.md:269` and `:603`.\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/README.md:67` names the same thirteen `/create:*` commands including `/create:sk-skill`, and `:194` answers the how-do-I question with the same name.\n- `.opencode/commands/create/sk-skill.md` and `.claude/commands/create/sk-skill.md` exist under the same name, so the two runtime command trees that mirror this group carry the renamed file rather than a stale `skill.md`.\n- `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt:28` restarts the workflow with `@markdown /create:sk-skill ...`, the exact name the README now gives.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Iteration numbering: this is the lineage's first iteration (the state log held only the run-initialized config row), so `iteration-001.md` is correct.\n- Diff base direction: the scope file prescribes a two-dot `origin/main..1c3d62def5a` README diff. The branch merged `origin/main` at `2b946c9e842`, so the endpoint diff is the branch's own rename and not main's movement; a merge-base-only diff would have hidden nothing because the file's two endpoints differ only in the rename.\n- Pre-existing prose: `README.md:599-611` count and group sentences predate this branch. They are context for the changed Create row, not branch findings; the two changed lines do not alter any count.\n- The changed line at `:269` also names eight other create commands. Each was resolved individually, because a rename that repaired one name could still leave a sibling broken in the same sentence.\n- `security` lens: the changed text is inert documentation. It adds no shell invocation, no path, no secret and no trust boundary, so the lens produced no candidate; that is a clean result, not skipped coverage.\n- `maintainability` lens: the new spelling appears in both places that describe the skill command, and no third README sentence retains the old spelling; a future reader has one name to search.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- **Command-name resolution:** all 44 `/group:name` tokens in `README.md` resolve to a Markdown file under `.skilled/commands`; the only README command names outside that tree are the four runtime-owned goal commands at `README.md:341` and `:613`, which are documented as runtime additions.\n- **Rename completeness:** the old token `/create:skill` (excluding `/create:skill-parent`) appears nowhere in `README.md`; both occurrences were updated in the same change.\n- **Create count:** `Create (13)` lists thirteen names and `.skilled/commands/create` holds thirteen command Markdown files (plus `README.txt` and the `assets/` folder).\n- **Mode support:** all thirteen create commands carry `[:auto|:confirm]` in their `argument-hint` and own both an `-auto.yaml` and a `-confirm.yaml` asset, so `README.md:269`'s \"Every one runs with `:auto` or with `:confirm`\" holds for the renamed command and its twelve siblings.\n- **Confirm semantics:** the renamed command's confirm workflow sets `approvals: step_by_step` and describes \"approval gates at each checkpoint\" (`create-skill-confirm.yaml:30,39-40`), matching the README's \"pause at each step\".\n- **Command behaviour claim:** `README.md:269` says the command \"creates or updates a skill\"; `create-skill-auto.yaml:113` sets `skill_path: .skilled/skills/` and the presentation contract offers `full-create`, `full-update`, `reference-only` and `asset-only`, so the README's scope is the shared skill tree rather than one runtime's copy.\n- **Doctor count:** the seventeen table rows at `README.md:646-662` match the seventeen command files in `.skilled/commands/doctor`.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- **A stale second `/create:skill` reference in the README:** `grep -n \"create:skill\" README.md` returns only the two renamed lines, both already `/create:sk-skill`.\n- **A broken command in the changed sentence:** all nine names in the `:269` sentence and all thirteen names in the `:603` list resolve to existing files.\n- **A wrong Create count after the rename:** the heading, the list and the folder each carry thirteen entries; renaming a file did not change the count.\n- **A command that exists only in the source tree:** the `.opencode` and `.claude` command mirrors carry `create/sk-skill.md`, so the README name is reachable on the runtime surfaces that mirror the group.\n- **A stale instruction inside the renamed command:** the presentation contract, the confirm workflow's completion actions and the group index all use `/create:sk-skill`; no old name remains in the commands tree.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: correctness and maintainability\n- Focus area: the two changed lines as claims rather than names, plus the counts and mode sentences they sit in, checked against the files they describe\n- Reason: traceability is swept; the remaining risk is a true-looking name attached to a false behaviour, count or mode claim\n- Rotation status: traceability complete; correctness, security and maintainability have a first pass and need a second read\n- Required evidence: per-claim file:line read with one concrete input per candidate\n- Recovery note: none\n\nReview verdict: PASS\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-7/iterations/iteration-001.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-7/iterations/iteration-001.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-7/iterations/iteration-001.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Review Iteration 001\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Lineage: `docs-7`, area `docs`.\\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder).\\n- Focus: traceability, with correctness, security and maintainability lenses applied to the same two changed README lines. The pass-seven operator focus is the docs area: this branch's net change to the root `README.md` against `origin/main`, where `/create:skill` was renamed `/create:sk-skill`, so every command name the README gives is checked against `.skilled/commands`. `review/review-brief-7.txt` and `review/review-scope-7.txt` were read first; this iteration covers the area they assign to `docs-7`.\\n- Diff base: `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff origin/main 1c3d62def5a -- README.md`, the command on line 1 of the scope file. It reports two lines changed, 2 insertions and 2 deletions: `README.md:269` and `README.md:603`.\\n- `steer.md` does not exist in the lineage directory, so no lead ruling applied.\\n- Recorded limits and the holdout rule were honoured: no prompt corpus was opened, no `git diff`/`show`/`log -p` ran over a path containing one, `score-command-transcripts.mjs --summary` was not run, and no CLI session store was read.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n| File | Lines read | What was checked |\\n|------|-----------|------------------|\\n| `README.md` | 266-271 | The changed extending-Skilled paragraph: the renamed `/create:sk-skill` and the remaining `/create:*` names, plus the `:auto`/`:confirm` sentence |\\n| `README.md` | 580-613 | The agent list and the whole commands section: all 44 names, the six group counts, and the changed Create list |\\n| `README.md` | 640-663 | The Doctor table, to test the `Doctor (17)` count against real files |\\n| `README.md` | 341 | The runtime goal-command paragraph, to confirm the four runtime-owned goal commands are outside the 44 |\\n| `.skilled/commands/README.txt` | 1-40 | The command tree's own six-group index and counts |\\n| `.skilled/commands/create/README.txt` | 50-95, 119-180 | The create group index rows, the command-map tree, and every example invocation of the renamed command |\\n| `.skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md` | 1-40 | The renamed router's frontmatter name, description, argument hint and owned assets |\\n| `.skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md` | 40-80 | The mode routing and execution targets for `:auto` and `:confirm` |\\n| `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/README.md` | 60-70, 190-198 | The sk-doc hub's thirteen-command sentence and its how-do-I answer naming `/create:sk-skill` |\\n\\nContext evidence (read-only, outside the docs scope path): `.skilled/commands/**` file inventory, `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt:1,28`, `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-auto.yaml:113`, `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-confirm.yaml:30,39-40`, `.opencode/commands/create/sk-skill.md`, `.claude/commands/create/sk-skill.md`.\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\\n|----------|--------|----------|\\n| `spec_code` | pass | Both changed lines name a command file that exists: `/create:sk-skill` resolves to `.skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md` and every other `/group:name` token in `README.md` resolves to `.skilled/commands/<group>/<name>.md` (44 of 44). The two changed lines agree with each other. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | notApplicable | The review target has no `checklist.md` at the packet root; the pass-seven brief and scope file are the operative checklist and both were read. |\\n| `skill_agent` | pass | The renamed command's own surfaces agree with the README name: `.skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md:1-13` routes `/create:sk-skill`, and `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt:1,28` presents the same name. |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | notApplicable | No agent body is in the docs scope; the command mirrors that do exist are recorded under Integration Evidence. |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | notApplicable | No feature-catalog claim is touched by the two changed README lines. |\\n| `playbook_capability` | notApplicable | No manual-testing-playbook claim is touched by the two changed README lines. |\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- `.skilled/commands/README.txt:21-35` gives the six-group table: create 13, deep 2, doctor 17, design 3, prompt 1, speckit 8, which sums to the README's `Forty-four commands ship in six groups` at `README.md:599`; `local-skilled-alignment.md` sits at the tree root and is not counted in the six groups.\\n- `.skilled/commands/create/README.txt:57` names `/create:sk-skill <skill-name> [operation] [type] [--path <dir>] [--chained] [:auto|:confirm]`, and `:88` maps `sk-skill.md` to `/create:sk-skill`; both agree with `README.md:269` and `:603`.\\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/README.md:67` names the same thirteen `/create:*` commands including `/create:sk-skill`, and `:194` answers the how-do-I question with the same name.\\n- `.opencode/commands/create/sk-skill.md` and `.claude/commands/create/sk-skill.md` exist under the same name, so the two runtime command trees that mirror this group carry the renamed file rather than a stale `skill.md`.\\n- `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt:28` restarts the workflow with `@markdown /create:sk-skill ...`, the exact name the README now gives.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- Iteration numbering: this is the lineage's first iteration (the state log held only the run-initialized config row), so `iteration-001.md` is correct.\\n- Diff base direction: the scope file prescribes a two-dot `origin/main..1c3d62def5a` README diff. The branch merged `origin/main` at `2b946c9e842`, so the endpoint diff is the branch's own rename and not main's movement; a merge-base-only diff would have hidden nothing because the file's two endpoints differ only in the rename.\\n- Pre-existing prose: `README.md:599-611` count and group sentences predate this branch. They are context for the changed Create row, not branch findings; the two changed lines do not alter any count.\\n- The changed line at `:269` also names eight other create commands. Each was resolved individually, because a rename that repaired one name could still leave a sibling broken in the same sentence.\\n- `security` lens: the changed text is inert documentation. It adds no shell invocation, no path, no secret and no trust boundary, so the lens produced no candidate; that is a clean result, not skipped coverage.\\n- `maintainability` lens: the new spelling appears in both places that describe the skill command, and no third README sentence retains the old spelling; a future reader has one name to search.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- **Command-name resolution:** all 44 `/group:name` tokens in `README.md` resolve to a Markdown file under `.skilled/commands`; the only README command names outside that tree are the four runtime-owned goal commands at `README.md:341` and `:613`, which are documented as runtime additions.\\n- **Rename completeness:** the old token `/create:skill` (excluding `/create:skill-parent`) appears nowhere in `README.md`; both occurrences were updated in the same change.\\n- **Create count:** `Create (13)` lists thirteen names and `.skilled/commands/create` holds thirteen command Markdown files (plus `README.txt` and the `assets/` folder).\\n- **Mode support:** all thirteen create commands carry `[:auto|:confirm]` in their `argument-hint` and own both an `-auto.yaml` and a `-confirm.yaml` asset, so `README.md:269`'s \\\"Every one runs with `:auto` or with `:confirm`\\\" holds for the renamed command and its twelve siblings.\\n- **Confirm semantics:** the renamed command's confirm workflow sets `approvals: step_by_step` and describes \\\"approval gates at each checkpoint\\\" (`create-skill-confirm.yaml:30,39-40`), matching the README's \\\"pause at each step\\\".\\n- **Command behaviour claim:** `README.md:269` says the command \\\"creates or updates a skill\\\"; `create-skill-auto.yaml:113` sets `skill_path: .skilled/skills/` and the presentation contract offers `full-create`, `full-update`, `reference-only` and `asset-only`, so the README's scope is the shared skill tree rather than one runtime's copy.\\n- **Doctor count:** the seventeen table rows at `README.md:646-662` match the seventeen command files in `.skilled/commands/doctor`.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- **A stale second `/create:skill` reference in the README:** `grep -n \\\"create:skill\\\" README.md` returns only the two renamed lines, both already `/create:sk-skill`.\\n- **A broken command in the changed sentence:** all nine names in the `:269` sentence and all thirteen names in the `:603` list resolve to existing files.\\n- **A wrong Create count after the rename:** the heading, the list and the folder each carry thirteen entries; renaming a file did not change the count.\\n- **A command that exists only in the source tree:** the `.opencode` and `.claude` command mirrors carry `create/sk-skill.md`, so the README name is reachable on the runtime surfaces that mirror the group.\\n- **A stale instruction inside the renamed command:** the presentation contract, the confirm workflow's completion actions and the group index all use `/create:sk-skill`; no old name remains in the commands tree.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: correctness and maintainability\\n- Focus area: the two changed lines as claims rather than names, plus the counts and mode sentences they sit in, checked against the files they describe\\n- Reason: traceability is swept; the remaining risk is a true-looking name attached to a false behaviour, count or mode claim\\n- Rotation status: traceability complete; correctness, security and maintainability have a first pass and need a second read\\n- Required evidence: per-claim file:line read with one concrete input per candidate\\n- Recovery note: none\\n\\nReview verdict: PASS\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-7/iterations/iteration-001.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794830418088,"end":1794830419001}}}}
