{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794830451336,"sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeKe3TiuKUBtJoOy","part":{"partID":"prt_1e43b4197001NqT5WutLpvjeM7","sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeKe3TiuKUBtJoOy","messageID":"msg_1e43b3376001EIz6cHX1pESwO6","type":"tool","id":"call_00_7bi5jag23ejq8c5m551lerga","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n- Resolving every `/group:name` token in `README.md` against `.skilled/commands/<group>/<name>.md` in one sweep: 44 of 44 resolve, so the rename question closed on evidence rather than on the two changed lines alone (iteration 1).\n- Reading the create group's own index (`README.txt:57,88`) and the sk-doc hub answer (`README.md:67,194`) beside the root README: the renamed name is consistent in the three docs a reader could follow, not just in the diff (iteration 1).\n- Checking the thirteen command files' `argument-hint` and asset triples to test the \"Every one runs with `:auto` or with `:confirm`\" sentence at `README.md:269`: the claim holds for all thirteen, including the renamed command (iteration 1).\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n- A first pass over the changed sentence treated the nine names as one claim; one of them (`/create:skill-parent`) shares the old prefix, so the sweep had to exclude the `skill-parent` token explicitly before the \"no old name remains\" result was trustworthy (iteration 1).","oldString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-7/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-7/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-7/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-7/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-7/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-7/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -56,13 +56,15 @@\n - Resolved: 0\n \n <!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n+- Resolving every `/group:name` token in `README.md` against `.skilled/commands/<group>/<name>.md` in one sweep: 44 of 44 resolve, so the rename question closed on evidence rather than on the two changed lines alone (iteration 1).\n+- Reading the create group's own index (`README.txt:57,88`) and the sk-doc hub answer (`README.md:67,194`) beside the root README: the renamed name is consistent in the three docs a reader could follow, not just in the diff (iteration 1).\n+- Checking the thirteen command files' `argument-hint` and asset triples to test the \"Every one runs with `:auto` or with `:confirm`\" sentence at `README.md:269`: the claim holds for all thirteen, including the renamed command (iteration 1).\n \n-\n ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n+- A first pass over the changed sentence treated the nine names as one claim; one of them (`/create:skill-parent`) shares the old prefix, so the sweep had to exclude the `skill-parent` token explicitly before the \"no old name remains\" result was trustworthy (iteration 1).\n \n-\n ---\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n","status":"modified","additions":4,"deletions":2}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-7/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\": \"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n- Resolving every `/group:name` token in