{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794830612688,"sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeKe3TiuKUBtJoOy","part":{"partID":"prt_1e43db6e8001I5R9nW0UvAOola","sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeKe3TiuKUBtJoOy","messageID":"msg_1e43da77800161P2oQqSUMVZxR","type":"tool","id":"call_00_42jlengwqdxpmxp4oamueehw","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"- Checking the thirteen command files' `argument-hint` and asset triples to test the \"Every one runs with `:auto` or with `:confirm`\" sentence at `README.md:269`: the claim holds for all thirteen, including the renamed command (iteration 1).\n- Comparing the `.opencode` create-command copies byte for byte with the canonical files: all thirteen match, so the runtime surface the README points at cannot drift from the documented command (iteration 2).\n- Sweeping the eight runtime trees for the renamed command's filename: `.claude` symlinks to it, `.opencode` copies it, and `.codex`/`.cursor`/`.pi`/`.dsh`/`.vibe` carry `create-sk-skill`, so the README name is reachable everywhere the group is mirrored (iteration 2).\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n- A first pass over the changed sentence treated the nine names as one claim; one of them (`/create:skill-parent`) shares the old prefix, so the sweep had to exclude the `skill-parent` token explicitly before the \"no old name remains\" result was trustworthy (iteration 1).\n- A runtime-folder assumption (that every runtime keeps a `commands/create` folder) was wrong for six of the eight trees; the sweep had to follow each runtime's own prompt or skill layout before the mirror result meant anything (iteration 2).","oldString":"- Checking the thirteen command files' `argument-hint` and asset triples to test the \"Every one runs with `:auto` or with `:confirm`\" sentence at `README.md:269`: the claim holds for all thirteen, including the renamed command (iteration 1).\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n- A first pass over the changed sentence treated the nine names as one claim; one of them (`/create:skill-parent`) shares the old prefix, so the sweep had to exclude the `skill-parent` token explicitly before the \"no old name remains\" result was trustworthy (iteration 1).","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-7/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-7/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-7/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-7/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-7/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-7/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -59,11 +59,14 @@\n ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n - Resolving every `/group:name` token in `README.md` against `.skilled/commands/<group>/<name>.md` in one sweep: 44 of 44 resolve, so the rename question closed on evidence rather than on the two changed lines alone (iteration 1).\n - Reading the create group's own index (`README.txt:57,88`) and the sk-doc hub answer (`README.md:67,194`) beside the root README: the renamed name is consistent in the three docs a reader could follow, not just in the diff (iteration 1).\n - Checking the thirteen command files' `argument-hint` and asset triples to test the \"Every one runs with `:auto` or with `:confirm`\" sentence at `README.md:269`: the claim holds for all thirteen, including the renamed command (iteration 1).\n+- Comparing the `.opencode` create-command copies byte for byte with the canonical files: all thirteen match, so the runtime surface the README points at cannot drift from the documented command (iteration 2).\n+- Sweeping the eight runtime trees for the renamed command's filename: `.claude` symlinks to it, `.opencode` copies it, and `.codex`/`.cursor`/`.pi`/`.dsh`/`.vibe` carry `create-sk-skill`, so the README name is reachable everywhere the group is mirrored (iteration 2).\n \n ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n - A first pass over the changed sentence treated the nine names as one claim; one of them (`/create:skill-parent`) shares the old prefix, so the sweep had to exclude the `skill-parent` token explicitly before the \"no old name remains\" result was trustworthy (iteration 1).\n+- A runtime-folder assumption (that every runtime keeps a `commands/create` folder) was wrong for six of the eight trees; the sweep had to follow each runtime's own prompt or skill layout before the mirror result meant anything (iteration 2).\n \n ---\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n","status":"modified","additions":3,"deletions":0}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-7/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\": \"- Checking the thirteen command files' `argument-hint` and asset triples to test the \\\"Every one runs with `:auto` or with `:confirm`\\\" sentence at `README.md:269`: the claim holds for all thirteen, including the renamed command (iteration 1).\\n- Comparing the `.opencode` create-command copies byte for byte with the canonical files: all thirteen match, so the runtime surface the README points at cannot drift from the documented command (iteration 2).\\n- Sweeping the eight runtime trees for the renamed command's filename: `.claude` symlinks to it, `.opencode` copies it, and `.codex`/`.cursor`/`.pi`/`.dsh`/`.vibe` carry `create-sk-skill`, so the README name is reachable everywhere the group is mirrored (iteration 2).\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n- A first pass over the changed sentence treated the nine names as one claim; one of them (`/create:skill-parent`) shares the old prefix, so the sweep had to exclude the `skill-parent` token explicitly before the \\\"no old name remains\\\" result was trustworthy (iteration 1).\\n- A runtime-folder assumption (that every runtime keeps a `commands/create` folder) was wrong for six of the eight trees; the sweep had to follow each runtime's own prompt or skill layout before the mirror result meant anything (iteration 2).\", \"oldString\": \"- Checking the thirteen command files' `argument-hint` and asset triples to test the \\\"Every one runs with `:auto` or with `:confirm`\\\" sentence at `README.md:269`: the claim holds for all thirteen, including the renamed command (iteration 1).\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n- A first pass over the changed sentence treated the nine names as one claim; one of them (`/create:skill-parent`) shares the old prefix, so the sweep had to exclude the `skill-parent` token explicitly before the \\\"no old name remains\\\" result was trustworthy (iteration 1).\", \"path\": \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-7/deep-review-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794830612200,"end":1794830612688}}}}
