{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794830732806,"sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeKe3TiuKUBtJoOy","part":{"partID":"prt_1e43f8c460012DVZ6lGJBBTng3","sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeKe3TiuKUBtJoOy","messageID":"msg_1e43f6290001KSZzJP5fVczhaF","type":"tool","id":"call_00_gpt1h30izts4cz9oi5dp5d18","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && rg -n \"create:skill[^-]\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/command-metadata.json .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/trigger-index -g '!**/command-prompts.jsonl' -g '!**/holdout-prompts.jsonl' -g '!**/behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl' 2>/dev/null | head -30"},"output":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md:106:A typed `/create:skill` now reads as `/create:sk-skill`. So a prompt that types the old name gets `sk-doc` with `/create:sk-skill (start)`. No command file answers to the old name. The retired name lives only in the `RETIRED_COMMANDS` table in `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts`. `runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` covers it. A path such as `docs/create:skill.md` still reads as no command.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md:206:**Breaking:** The command row `command-create-skill` is now `command-create-sk-skill`. Its slash markers are now `/create:sk-skill`. A typed `/create:skill` reads as `/create:sk-skill`, as Brief Commands above says. The rename itself is in the `sk-doc` v2.10.0.0 entry.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md:251:- **If you type `/create:skill`:** type `/create:sk-skill` instead. The old name has no command file. A typed `/create:skill` still reads as `/create:sk-skill`.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:217:  '/create:skill': '/create:sk-skill',\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:460:    expect(typedCommandIn('/create:skill')).toBe('/create:sk-skill');\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:461:    expect(typedCommandIn('/create:skill make a linting skill')).toBe('/create:sk-skill');\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:462:    expect(typedCommandForTop('sk-doc', '/create:skill')).toEqual({\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:470:    expect(typedCommandIn('open docs/create:skill.md')).toBeUndefined();\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md:106:A typed `/create:skill` now reads as `/create:sk-skill`. So a prompt that types the old name gets `sk-doc` with `/create:sk-skill (start)`. No command file answers to the old name. The retired name lives only in the `RETIRED_COMMANDS` table in `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts`. `runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` covers it. A path such as `docs/create:skill.md` still reads as no command.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md:206:**Breaking:** The command row `command-create-skill` is now `command-create-sk-skill`. Its slash markers are now `/create:sk-skill`. A typed `/create:skill` reads as `/create:sk-skill`, as Brief Commands above says. The rename itself is in the `sk-doc` v2.10.0.0 entry.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md:251:- **If you type `/create:skill`:** type `/create:sk-skill` instead. The old name has no command file. A typed `/create:skill` still reads as `/create:sk-skill`.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:217:  '/create:skill': '/create:sk-skill',\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:460:    expect(typedCommandIn('/create:skill')).toBe('/create:sk-skill');\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:461:    expect(typedCommandIn('/create:skill make a linting skill')).toBe('/create:sk-skill');\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:462:    expect(typedCommandForTop('sk-doc', '/create:skill')).toEqual({\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:470:    expect(typedCommandIn('open docs/create:skill.md')).toBeUndefined();\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && rg -n \\\"create:skill[^-]\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/command-metadata.json .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/trigger-index -g '!**/command-prompts.jsonl' -g '!**/holdout-prompts.jsonl' -g '!**/behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl' 2>/dev/null | head -30\"}"},"time":{"start":1794830732358,"end":1794830732806}}}}
