{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794830748363,"sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeKe3TiuKUBtJoOy","part":{"partID":"prt_1e43fc9dd001HUolIjsZ7Ijn5X","sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeKe3TiuKUBtJoOy","messageID":"msg_1e43f9acb001Bambj2lQDzv3NC","type":"tool","id":"call_00_g7o9t35gpa7n7u4k342w1t49","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && git show origin/main:README.md | sed -n 269p; git show origin/main:README.md | sed -n 603p; echo \"=== rename commit README diff\"; git show 74d3744e641 -- README.md | head -40"},"output":"Each kind also has a `/create` command for when you want the workflow directly. `/create:skill` creates or updates a skill, and `/create:skill-parent` scaffolds a parent hub with its modes. `/create:agent` and `/create:command` cover agents and slash commands. `/create:readme`, `/create:changelog`, `/create:goal` and `/create:repo-rule` cover the documents around them. Every one runs with `:auto` or with `:confirm` to pause at each step.\n**Create (13).** `/create:skill`, `/create:skill-parent`, `/create:agent`, `/create:command`, `/create:readme`, `/create:changelog`, `/create:feature-catalog`, `/create:manual-testing-playbook`, `/create:goal`, `/create:benchmark`, `/create:diff`, `/create:repo-rule` and `/create:with-human-voice`. These scaffold or revise one kind of artifact to the sk-doc standards.\n=== rename commit README diff\ncommit 74d3744e64164596fac74b0f82e33144b220a2e7\nAuthor: Michel Kerkmeester <82775228+MichelKerkmeester@users.noreply.github.com>\nDate:   Fri Nov 13 17:52:46 2026 +0100\n\n    feat(system-skill-advisor): rename the create skill command and offer the doctor helper\n    \n    The command /create:skill is now /create:sk-skill on every runtime, with\n    no alias. A command file named skill.md makes Claude Code read its\n    folder as one skill and hide the other commands in it, an open upstream\n    bug. With the new file name Claude Code lists all 44 tracked commands,\n    up from 32. The mirror check drops its allowlist and fails on a command\n    file named skill.md in any capitalisation. The sk-doc hub moves to\n    2.10.0.0 with a changelog entry that calls out the break.\n    \n    A doctor prompt that says a tool does not show up or appear now counts\n    as a strong problem cue, so the brief names /doctor:helper beside the\n    skills. The idioms \"appear to\" and \"up-to-date\" stay out of the cue.\n    \n    The Gate 2 direct call in AGENTS.md sends the request on stdin, so a\n    prompt never sits in the process table. Its manifest and the Cursor\n    rule carry the same line.\n    \n    Five commands gain intent phrases: four doctor routes and the spec\n    search. On the real embedder, plain holdout reach reads 5 of 44, up\n    from 3, with typed recall and false offers unchanged.\n    \n    A brief-cost run points each hook child's temp folder at its sandbox,\n    so it writes nothing into the shared health log.\n    \n    Floors held: typed recall 24/44, false offers 0/35, scorer eval\n    [160,50,21,5]. Suite: 183 files, 1,758 passed. Doctor tests 1,189,\n    0 failed.\n    \n    Spec: system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default\n    Commit-Id: 0013878\n\ndiff --git a/README.md b/README.md\nindex 7bb76ab9fdc..a027d982d85 100644\n--- a/README.md\n+++ b/README.md\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Each kind also has a `/create` command for when you want the workflow directly. `/create:skill` creates or updates a skill, and `/create:skill-parent` scaffolds a parent hub with its modes. `/create:agent` and `/create:command` cover agents and slash commands. `/create:readme`, `/create:changelog`, `/create:goal` and `/create:repo-rule` cover the documents around them. Every one runs with `:auto` or with `:confirm` to pause at each step.\n**Create (13).** `/create:skill`, `/create:skill-parent`, `/create:agent`, `/create:command`, `/create:readme`, `/create:changelog`, `/create:feature-catalog`, `/create:manual-testing-playbook`, `/create:goal`, `/create:benchmark`, `/create:diff`, `/create:repo-rule` and `/create:with-human-voice`. These scaffold or revise one kind of artifact to the sk-doc standards.\n=== rename commit README diff\ncommit 74d3744e64164596fac74b0f82e33144b220a2e7\nAuthor: Michel Kerkmeester <82775228+MichelKerkmeester@users.noreply.github.com>\nDate:   Fri Nov 13 17:52:46 2026 +0100\n\n    feat(system-skill-advisor): rename the create skill command and offer the doctor helper\n    \n    The command /create:skill is now /create:sk-skill on every runtime, with\n    no alias. A command file named skill.md makes Claude Code read its\n    folder as one skill and hide the other commands in it, an open upstream\n    bug. With the new file name Claude Code lists all 44 tracked commands,\n    up from 32. The mirror check drops its allowlist and fails on a command\n    file named skill.md in any capitalisation. The sk-doc hub moves to\n    2.10.0.0 with a changelog entry that calls out the break.\n    \n    A doctor prompt that says a tool does not show up or appear now counts\n    as a strong problem cue, so the brief names /doctor:helper beside the\n    skills. The idioms \"appear to\" and \"up-to-date\" stay out of the cue.\n    \n    The Gate 2 direct call in AGENTS.md sends the request on stdin, so a\n    prompt never sits in the process table. Its manifest and the Cursor\n    rule carry the same line.\n    \n    Five commands gain intent phrases: four doctor routes and the spec\n    search. On the real embedder, plain holdout reach reads 5 of 44, up\n    from 3, with typed recall and false offers unchanged.\n    \n    A brief-cost run points each hook child's temp folder at its sandbox,\n    so it writes nothing into the shared health log.\n    \n    Floors held: typed recall 24/44, false offers 0/35, scorer eval\n    [160,50,21,5]. Suite: 183 files, 1,758 passed. Doctor tests 1,189,\n    0 failed.\n    \n    Spec: system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default\n    Commit-Id: 0013878\n\ndiff --git a/README.md b/README.md\nindex 7bb76ab9fdc..a027d982d85 100644\n--- a/README.md\n+++ b/README.md\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && git show origin/main:README.md | sed -n 269p; git show origin/main:README.md | sed -n 603p; echo \\\"=== rename commit README diff\\\"; git show 74d3744e641 -- README.md | head -40\"}"},"time":{"start":1794830748125,"end":1794830748363}}}}
