{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794830780071,"sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeKe3TiuKUBtJoOy","part":{"partID":"prt_1e4404580001I46146Uuk1LFt6","sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeKe3TiuKUBtJoOy","messageID":"msg_1e44031cd001iU76DjtyaCFrtT","type":"tool","id":"call_00_6yl8lknldx39av9ih9mc9ly6","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"- Sweeping the eight runtime trees for the renamed command's filename: `.claude` symlinks to it, `.opencode` copies it, and `.codex`/`.cursor`/`.pi`/`.dsh`/`.vibe` carry `create-sk-skill`, so the README name is reachable everywhere the group is mirrored (iteration 2).\n- Proving the rename at blob level after `STUCK_RECOVERY`: `git show 1c3d62def5a:README.md` carries the new name at both lines while `origin/main` carries the old one, and the introducing commit `74d3744e641` is an ancestor of the reviewed revision, so the change is not a working-tree artifact or a later revert (iteration 3).\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n- A first pass over the changed sentence treated the nine names as one claim; one of them (`/create:skill-parent`) shares the old prefix, so the sweep had to exclude the `skill-parent` token explicitly before the \"no old name remains\" result was trustworthy (iteration 1).\n- A runtime-folder assumption (that every runtime keeps a `commands/create` folder) was wrong for six of the eight trees; the sweep had to follow each runtime's own prompt or skill layout before the mirror result meant anything (iteration 2).\n- Two clean iterations tripped the stuck counter (`STUCK_RECOVERY` at iteration 2); the loop only advances by changing the unit of evidence, which cost an iteration that a finding-bearing area would have spent on new code (iteration 3).","oldString":"- Sweeping the eight runtime trees for the renamed command's filename: `.claude` symlinks to it, `.opencode` copies it, and `.codex`/`.cursor`/`.pi`/`.dsh`/`.vibe` carry `create-sk-skill`, so the README name is reachable everywhere the group is mirrored (iteration 2).\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n- A first pass over the changed sentence treated the nine names as one claim; one of them (`/create:skill-parent`) shares the old prefix, so the sweep had to exclude the `skill-parent` token explicitly before the \"no old name remains\" result was trustworthy (iteration 1).\n- A runtime-folder assumption (that every runtime keeps a `commands/create` folder) was wrong for six of the eight trees; the sweep had to follow each runtime's own prompt or skill layout before the mirror result meant anything (iteration 2).","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-7/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-7/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-7/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-7/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-7/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-7/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -61,12 +61,14 @@\n - Reading the create group's own index (`README.txt:57,88`) and the sk-doc hub answer (`README.md:67,194`) beside the root README: the renamed name is consistent in the three docs a reader could follow, not just in the diff (iteration 1).\n - Checking the thirteen command files' `argument-hint` and asset triples to test the \"Every one runs with `:auto` or with `:confirm`\" sentence at `README.md:269`: the claim holds for all thirteen, including the renamed command (iteration 1).\n - Compari