{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794830886299,"sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeKe3TiuKUBtJoOy","part":{"partID":"prt_1e441e3c4001IHVSP55nX23wHZ","sessionID":"ses_e1bcb8a74ffeKe3TiuKUBtJoOy","messageID":"msg_1e441aca50018EGSzI7E3BlNQC","type":"tool","id":"call_00_ixqotqgcr13u2b1cr6p6owjz","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Report - docs-7\n\nLineage: `docs-7`, area `docs`, code review pass seven.\nReview target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder).\nScope: `README.md`, the root README's net change against `origin/main` at `1c3d62def5a`.\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\n\n**Verdict: PASS.** No active P0, P1 or P2 finding exists. `hasAdvisories` is false.\n\n| Measure | Value |\n|---------|-------|\n| Active P0 | 0 |\n| Active P1 | 0 |\n| Active P2 | 0 |\n| Iterations run | 3 of 3 |\n| Terminal stop | `maxIterationsReached` |\n| Required terminal gates | evidence pass, scope pass, coverage pass (`coverage-complete`) |\n| Stop-blocking gate row | `hotspotSaturationGate` false because the coverage graph is empty; not a required gate |\n| Release readiness | `converged` |\n\nThe reviewed change is two lines of `README.md` (`:269` and `:603`), a complete rename from `/create:skill` to `/create:sk-skill`. The reviewed blob carries the new name in both places, `origin/main` carries the old one, and every command name the README gives resolves to a file under `.skilled/commands` at the reviewed revision.\n\n## 2. Planning Trigger\n\nPASS routes to `/create:changelog` per the review verdict table; `/speckit:plan` is not triggered. There is no remediation workstream because the area has no active finding: the rename reached both README surfaces and the command tree, and the counts and mode sentences the changed lines sit in are true. A changelog follow-up would only record that pass seven found the docs area clean.\n\n## 3. Active Finding Registry\n\nNone. The findings registry holds zero open and zero resolved findings, and the three iteration narratives record no finding at any severity.\n\n## 4. Remediation Workstreams\n\nNone. No defect, documentation gap or validation gap was confirmed inside the docs scope.\n\n## 5. Spec Seed\n\nNo spec delta is needed. The reviewed change matches the packet's intent: the command is renamed on every runtime and the root README names the new command. The packet's own spec is unchanged by this review.\n\n## 6. Plan Seed\n\nNo plan is needed. Nothing in the docs area requires an implementation step.\n\n## 7. Traceability Status\n\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Evidence |\n|----------|-------|--------|----------|\n| `spec_code` | core | pass | `README.md:269,603` and the reviewed tree's command folder agree; 44 of 44 README command names resolve |\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | notApplicable | No `checklist.md` at the packet root; the pass-seven brief and scope file are the operative checklist |\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | pass | The command router, its confirm workflow, its presentation contract and the create group index all use `/create:sk-skill` |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | notApplicable | No agent body in the docs scope |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | notApplicable | No feature-catalog claim touched |\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | No playbook claim touched |\n\nCore required: 2. Core executed: 2. Gating failures: 0.\n\n## 8. Deferred Items\n\n- **Graphless hotspot saturation:** the coverage graph has no nodes for this lineage (`nodeCount: 0`), so `hotspotSaturationGate` reports false and appears in `blockedBy`. It is not one of the three required terminal gates, and the terminal gate rows pass. It is recorded here rather than repaired, because building a graph is outside this lineage's write surface.\n- **Recorded pass-seven limits not re-reported:** the `:auto.md` suffix reading, the `node -e` arrow redirect, `isolation-check.sh` being macOS only, `started` versus `offered` not rebuilding from `readOnly`, and older goal rows keeping old-rule figures. None applies to the two changed README lines, and no new input breaks any of them.\n- **Pre-existing context, not a branch finding:** `.skilled/commands/local-skilled-alignment.md` is a command file at the commands-tree root. The README's \"Forty-four commands ship in six groups\" is scoped to the six groups, and the README's runtime-goal note at `:613` explains commands that live outside them, so the sentence is accurate at the reviewed revision.\n\n## 9. Audit Appendix\n\n### Iterations\n\n| Iteration | Focus | Dimensions | Findings | newFindingsRatio | Status |\n|-----------|-------|------------|----------|------------------|--------|\n| 1 | traceability | correctness, security, traceability, maintainability | 0 | 0.0 | complete |\n| 2 | correctness-maintainability | correctness, security, traceability, maintainability | 0 | 0.0 | complete |\n| 3 | recovery-provenance | correctness, security, traceability, maintainability | 0 | 0.0 | complete |\n\n### Dimension Coverage\n\n| Dimension | Last Iteration | Evidence |\n|-----------|----------------|----------|\n| correctness | 3 | Counts, mode sentence and command behavior verified against the files |\n| security | 3 | Changed text is inert; the renamed token is a fixed command name, and the retired name is a fixed mapping |\n| traceability | 3 | Blob-level, tree-level and commit-level rename provenance |\n| maintainability | 3 | One spelling across root README, group index, sk-doc README, presentation and workflows |\n\n### Convergence Evidence\n\n- `missingDimensions`: none.\n- `coverageAge`: 2 (all four dimensions were first covered in iteration 1).\n- `traceabilityCovered`: true.\n- `weightedStopScore`: 1.\n- `stop_decision.decision`: `STOP`, `stopReason`: `maxIterationsReached`.\n- `blockedBy`: `hotspotSaturationGate` (graph unavailable); no required gate is in that list.\n- `STUCK_RECOVERY` fired after iteration 2 because two clean iterations reached the stuck threshold; iteration 3 answered it with a different evidence unit (commit graph) and still produced no finding.\n\n### Terminal Gates\n\n| Gate | Status | Reason code |\n|------|--------|-------------|\n| evidence | pass | `all-findings-cited` |\n| scope | pass | `all-findings-in-scope` |\n| coverage | pass | `coverage-complete` |\n\n### Evidence Sources\n\n- `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff origin/main 1c3d62def5a -- README.md` (two hunks, 2 insertions and 2 deletions).\n- `git show 1c3d62def5a:README.md` lines 269 and 603; `git show origin/main:README.md` at the same lines.\n- `git show --stat 74d3744e641`; `git merge-base --is-ancestor 74d3744e641 1c3d62def5a`.\n- `git ls-tree -r --name-only 1c3d62def5a .skilled/commands/create`.\n- `.skilled/commands/README.txt:21-35`, `.skilled/commands/create/README.txt:57,88,119-180`, `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/README.md:67,194`.\n- `.skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md`, `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-auto.yaml:113`, `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-confirm.yaml:30,39-40,626-630`.\n- `.opencode/commands/create/*.md` (byte equality), `.claude/commands/create/sk-skill.md` (symlink), `.codex`/`.cursor`/`.pi`/`.dsh`/`.vibe` prompt filenames.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:217`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md:206,251`.\n\n### Artifacts\n\n- Iterations: `iterations/iteration-001.md`, `iterations/iteration-002.md`, `iterations/iteration-003.md`.\n- Deltas: `deltas/iter-001.jsonl`, `deltas/iter-002.jsonl`, `deltas/iter-003.jsonl`.\n- State: `deep-review-state.jsonl` (gateway projection), `deep-review-findings-registry.json`, `deep-review-dashboard.md`, `deep-review-strategy.md`.\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-7/review-report.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-7/review-report.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-7/review-report.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Review Report - docs-7\\n\\nLineage: `docs-7`, area `docs`, code review pass seven.\\nReview target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder).\\nScope: `README.md`, the root README's net change against `origin/main` at `1c3d62def5a`.\\n\\n## 1. Executive Summary\\n\\n**Verdict: PASS.** No active P0, P1 or P2 finding exists. `hasAdvisories` is false.\\n\\n| Measure | Value |\\n|---------|-------|\\n| Active P0 | 0 |\\n| Active P1 | 0 |\\n| Active P2 | 0 |\\n| Iterations run | 3 of 3 |\\n| Terminal stop | `maxIterationsReached` |\\n| Required terminal gates | evidence pass, scope pass, coverage pass (`coverage-complete`) |\\n| Stop-blocking gate row | `hotspotSaturationGate` false because the coverage graph is empty; not a required gate |\\n| Release readiness | `converged` |\\n\\nThe reviewed change is two lines of `README.md` (`:269` and `:603`), a complete rename from `/create:skill` to `/create:sk-skill`. The reviewed blob carries the new name in both places, `origin/main` carries the old one, and every command name the README gives resolves to a file under `.skilled/commands` at the reviewed revision.\\n\\n## 2. Planning Trigger\\n\\nPASS routes to `/create:changelog` per the review verdict table; `/speckit:plan` is not triggered. There is no remediation workstream because the area has no active finding: the rename reached both README surfaces and the command tree, and the counts and mode sentences the changed lines sit in are true. A changelog follow-up would only record that pass seven found the docs area clean.\\n\\n## 3. Active Finding Registry\\n\\nNone. The findings registry holds zero open and zero resolved findings, and the three iteration narratives record no finding at any severity.\\n\\n## 4. Remediation Workstreams\\n\\nNone. No defect, documentation gap or validation gap was confirmed inside the docs scope.\\n\\n## 5. Spec Seed\\n\\nNo spec delta is needed. The reviewed change matches the packet's intent: the command is renamed on every runtime and the root README names the new command. The packet's own spec is unchanged by this review.\\n\\n## 6. Plan Seed\\n\\nNo plan is needed. Nothing in the docs area requires an implementation step.\\n\\n## 7. Traceability Status\\n\\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Evidence |\\n|----------|-------|--------|----------|\\n| `spec_code` | core | pass | `README.md:269,603` and the reviewed tree's command folder agree; 44 of 44 README command names resolve |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | notApplicable | No `checklist.md` at the packet root; the pass-seven brief and scope file are the operative checklist |\\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | pass | The command router, its confirm workflow, its presentation contract and the create group index all use `/create:sk-skill` |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | notApplicable | No agent body in the docs scope |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | notApplicable | No feature-catalog claim touched |\\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | No playbook claim touched |\\n\\nCore required: 2. Core executed: 2. Gating failures: 0.\\n\\n## 8. Deferred Items\\n\\n- **Graphless hotspot saturation:** the coverage graph has no nodes for this lineage (`nodeCount: 0`), so `hotspotSaturationGate` reports false and appears in `blockedBy`. It is not one of the three required terminal gates, and the terminal gate rows pass. It is recorded here rather than repaired, because building a graph is outside this lineage's write surface.\\n- **Recorded pass-seven limits not re-reported:** the `:auto.md` suffix reading, the `node -e` arrow redirect, `isolation-check.sh` being macOS only, `started` versus `offered` not rebuilding from `readOnly`, and older goal rows keeping old-rule figures. None applies to the two changed README lines, and no new input breaks any of them.\\n- **Pre-existing context, not a branch finding:** `.skilled/commands/local-skilled-alignment.md` is a command file at the commands-tree root. The README's \\\"Forty-four commands ship in six groups\\\" is scoped to the six groups, and the README's runtime-goal note at `:613` explains commands that live outside them, so the sentence is accurate at the reviewed revision.\\n\\n## 9. Audit Appendix\\n\\n### Iterations\\n\\n| Iteration | Focus | Dimensions | Findings | newFindingsRatio | Status |\\n|-----------|-------|------------|----------|------------------|--------|\\n| 1 | traceability | correctness, security, traceability, maintainability | 0 | 0.0 | complete |\\n| 2 | correctness-maintainability | correctness, security, traceability, maintainability | 0 | 0.0 | complete |\\n| 3 | recovery-provenance | correctness, security, traceability, maintainability | 0 | 0.0 | complete |\\n\\n### Dimension Coverage\\n\\n| Dimension | Last Iteration | Evidence |\\n|-----------|----------------|----------|\\n| correctness | 3 | Counts, mode sentence and command behavior verified against the files |\\n| security | 3 | Changed text is inert; the renamed token is a fixed command name, and the retired name is a fixed mapping |\\n| traceability | 3 | Blob-level, tree-level and commit-level rename provenance |\\n| maintainability | 3 | One spelling across root README, group index, sk-doc README, presentation and workflows |\\n\\n### Convergence Evidence\\n\\n- `missingDimensions`: none.\\n- `coverageAge`: 2 (all four dimensions were first covered in iteration 1).\\n- `traceabilityCovered`: true.\\n- `weightedStopScore`: 1.\\n- `stop_decision.decision`: `STOP`, `stopReason`: `maxIterationsReached`.\\n- `blockedBy`: `hotspotSaturationGate` (graph unavailable); no required gate is in that list.\\n- `STUCK_RECOVERY` fired after iteration 2 because two clean iterations reached the stuck threshold; iteration 3 answered it with a different evidence unit (commit graph) and still produced no finding.\\n\\n### Terminal Gates\\n\\n| Gate | Status | Reason code |\\n|------|--------|-------------|\\n| evidence | pass | `all-findings-cited` |\\n| scope | pass | `all-findings-in-scope` |\\n| coverage | pass | `coverage-complete` |\\n\\n### Evidence Sources\\n\\n- `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff origin/main 1c3d62def5a -- README.md` (two hunks, 2 insertions and 2 deletions).\\n- `git show 1c3d62def5a:README.md` lines 269 and 603; `git show origin/main:README.md` at the same lines.\\n- `git show --stat 74d3744e641`; `git merge-base --is-ancestor 74d3744e641 1c3d62def5a`.\\n- `git ls-tree -r --name-only 1c3d62def5a .skilled/commands/create`.\\n- `.skilled/commands/README.txt:21-35`, `.skilled/commands/create/README.txt:57,88,119-180`, `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/README.md:67,194`.\\n- `.skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md`, `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-auto.yaml:113`, `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-confirm.yaml:30,39-40,626-630`.\\n- `.opencode/commands/create/*.md` (byte equality), `.claude/commands/create/sk-skill.md` (symlink), `.codex`/`.cursor`/`.pi`/`.dsh`/`.vibe` prompt filenames.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:217`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md:206,251`.\\n\\n### Artifacts\\n\\n- Iterations: `iterations/iteration-001.md`, `iterations/iteration-002.md`, `iterations/iteration-003.md`.\\n- Deltas: `deltas/iter-001.jsonl`, `deltas/iter-002.jsonl`, `deltas/iter-003.jsonl`.\\n- State: `deep-review-state.jsonl` (gateway projection), `deep-review-findings-registry.json`, `deep-review-dashboard.md`, `deep-review-strategy.md`.\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/docs-7/review-report.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794830885828,"end":1794830886299}}}}
